WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.580
And we're best friends.
我们也是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们专门为你制作了《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:24.330
Good morning.
早上好。

9
00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:25.510
Good morning.
早上好。

10
00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:26.390
Good afternoon.
下午好。

11
00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:27.270
Good evening.
晚上好。

12
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.410
You're very peppy for such a serious subject.
面对这么严肃的话题，你还真是活力十足啊。

13
00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:34.510
I am really excited about this episode.
我对这一集感到非常兴奋。

14
00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:36.370
Everyone, it's murder.
各位，是谋杀案。

15
00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:38.190
Oh, dun-dun-dun.
噢，当当当。

16
00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:44.670
Season 6, Episode 10, written by Daniel Chun and directed by Greg Daniels.
第六季第十集，由丹尼尔·春编剧，格雷格·丹尼尔斯执导。

17
00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:48.450
And we have a special treat this week for you for our summary.
本周我们的剧情梗概有一个特别惊喜要送给大家。

18
00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:49.430
We do.
没错。

19
00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:54.010
Okay, so you guys, you know I have a big Southern family.
好了，大家知道我有一个庞大的南方大家庭。

20
00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:56.330
We're spread out between Louisiana and Texas.
我们分散在路易斯安那州和德克萨斯州。

21
00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.290
And I know it's not Savannah, Georgia.
我知道这和佐治亚州的萨凡纳不一样。

22
00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:03.030
But my sister, Billie Jo, has a great Southern accent.
但我妹妹比利·乔有很地道的南方口音。

23
00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:05.370
And I asked her to read our summary today.
我请她今天来读我们的剧情梗概。

24
00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:06.810
And she did.
她答应了。

25
00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:07.690
Here it is.
就是这个。

26
00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:10.570
I do declare there's been a murder.
我郑重声明，发生了一起谋杀案。

27
00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:18.250
Michael attempts to distract his employees with a murder mystery party after everyone hears rumors that the company might be going bankrupt.
在听到公司可能破产的传言后，迈克尔试图用一场谋杀之谜派对来分散员工的注意力。

28
00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:23.890
Jim wants everyone to keep walking and is frustrated by Michael's game.
吉姆希望大家继续工作，对迈克尔的游戏感到沮丧。

29
00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:28.170
Meanwhile, Andy attempts to ask Aaron out on a date.
与此同时，安迪试图约艾琳出去约会。

30
00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:30.750
Angela, she nailed it.
安吉拉，她读得太棒了。

31
00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:31.990
She nailed it.
太棒了。

32
00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:34.250
Jenna, I was so tickled by this.
珍娜，我被逗乐了。

33
00:01:34.370 --> 00:01:36.250
I knew I wanted someone in my family.
我知道我想找我家里的人来读。

34
00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.910
Because this episode partly takes place in Savannah, Georgia.
因为这一集的部分情节发生在佐治亚州的萨凡纳。

35
00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:40.350
Yes.
是的。

36
00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:44.450
So I knew I would want someone from my Southern family to give the summary a go.
所以我知道我想找我南方家里的某个人来尝试一下梗概。

37
00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:45.530
And thank you, Billie.
谢谢你，比利。

38
00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:47.350
Thank you, Billie, for giving it a shot.
谢谢你，比利，愿意尝试一下。

39
00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:49.430
Well, she can do the summary anytime, Ange.
嗯，她随时都可以来读梗概，安吉。

40
00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:50.950
Billie Jo, did you hear that?
比利·乔，你听到了吗？

41
00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:53.690
But right now, she's like, no, no, no, no, no.
但现在她肯定在说，不，不，不，不，不。

42
00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:55.170
Somewhere she's yelling, no, no, no.
她肯定在某处大喊，不，不，不。

43
00:01:56.570 --> 00:01:58.530
Well, let's get into fast facts.
好了，让我们进入快讯环节。

44
00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:04.830
Fast fact number one is all about our new writer for this episode, Daniel Chun.
第一个快讯是关于我们这一集的新编剧，丹尼尔·春。

45
00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:06.130
We know him as Danny.
我们叫他丹尼。

46
00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:09.330
He started on the writing staff for season six.
他从第六季开始加入编剧团队。

47
00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:11.170
He was a supervising producer.
他当时是监制。

48
00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:13.590
And this was his first script.
这是他写的第一个剧本。

49
00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:18.450
Danny had previously written on The Simpsons for six years.
丹尼之前在《辛普森一家》写了六年剧本。

50
00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.610
I was able to get back in touch with him, which was so fun.
我联系上了他，这真是太有趣了。

51
00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:25.870
And he told me that he knew a lot of the office writers socially,
他告诉我，他私下里认识办公室里很多编剧，

52
00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.030
just through the comedy writing community.
就是通过喜剧写作圈子认识的。

53
00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:30.470
He knew BJ for a long time.
他认识BJ很久了。

54
00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.150
He said that he loved being at The Simpsons,
他说他很喜欢在《辛普森一家》工作，

55
00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:37.790
but he kind of felt like 80% of working on that show was just punching up jokes.
但他觉得在那部剧里80%的工作只是在润色笑话。

56
00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.350
Unless you were the showrunner.
除非你是剧集主管。

57
00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:43.090
So he didn't get to do a lot of long-form writing there, I guess.
所以我猜他在那里没能做太多长篇写作。

58
00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:45.930
He said he was really hungry for a different challenge.
他说他真的很渴望接受不同的挑战。

59
00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:48.870
BJ had always been a big supporter of his writing,
BJ一直都很支持他的写作，

60
00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:54.390
and he showed Mindy and Paul some stuff that Danny had written just for fun on MySpace.
他给敏迪和保罗看了些丹尼在MySpace上纯属娱乐写的作品。

61
00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:55.690
Remember MySpace?
还记得MySpace吗？

62
00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:56.690
Oh, my God, yeah.
天哪，记得。

63
00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:59.730
He said that gives you a sense of how long ago this was.
他说这让你感觉到那是多久以前的事了。

64
00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:03.410
But the stuff he had written on MySpace got him a meeting.
但他写在MySpace上的东西让他获得了一次面谈机会。

65
00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:08.130
They brought him in, and that's how he got hired to be one of our writers for season six.
他们把他叫了过去，这就是他如何被聘为我们第六季编剧之一的经过。

66
00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:10.110
See, guys, you never know.
看吧，伙计们，你永远不知道会发生什么。

67
00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:11.430
You never know.
你永远不知道。

68
00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:16.990
Yeah, all that stuff that you're writing, if it's a blog, if it's a vlog, I don't even know.
没错，你写的那些东西，不管是博客还是视频博客，我甚至都不知道叫什么。

69
00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:18.330
You're creating it.
你正在创作它。

70
00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:19.550
All the logs out there.
外面所有的那些“志”。

71
00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:20.190
All of them.
所有的那些。

72
00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:21.370
Someone could see it.
可能会有人看到它。

73
00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:21.950
Yes.
是的。

74
00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:30.590
So, fast fact number two, I was able to talk to Danny a little bit about the inspiration for this episode of murder.
那么，第二个速记事实，我能和丹尼聊了聊这一集谋杀案的灵感来源。

75
00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:32.110
What was it?
是什么？

76
00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:35.330
He said this was a card on the wall.
他说这是墙上的一张卡片。

77
00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:36.830
What did the card say?
卡片上写了什么？

78
00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:41.170
The card said, Michael makes everyone play a murder mystery game.
卡片上写着：迈克尔让每个人玩谋杀之谜游戏。

79
00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:45.290
It was one of the pitches they had come up with over the summer.
这是他们夏天想出的点子之一。

80
00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:48.590
He also remembered a card that never got made.
他还记得一张从未被拍出来的卡片。

81
00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.010
It was this.
是这个。

82
00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:54.330
They go on a ski trip, and someone makes a huge stain on the wall.
他们去滑雪旅行，有人在墙上弄出了一个巨大的污渍。

83
00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:55.650
Ew.
呃。

84
00:03:56.010 --> 00:04:00.690
I know, but he was pointing out, like, this is how simple a card could be.
我知道，但他指出，卡片可以简单到这种程度。

85
00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:07.470
But they picked this one, and then they had to figure out how, why, what happens?
但他们选了这一张，然后他们必须弄清楚怎么回事、为什么、发生了什么？

86
00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:09.070
How is this a whole episode?
这怎么能拍成一整集？

87
00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:14.810
So, on Mom Detectives, a card could be two ladies on a train with a succulent.
所以，在《妈妈侦探》里，一张卡片可能就是两个女士带着一盆多肉植物在火车上。

88
00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:15.550
Yes!
没错！

89
00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:17.230
And that has to be a whole episode.
那也得拍成一整集。

90
00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:17.910
That's an episode.
那也是一集。

91
00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:18.450
Yeah.
是啊。

92
00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:20.650
And you have to turn that into something.
你必须把它变成点什么东西。

93
00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:20.930
Yeah.
没错。

94
00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:29.290
Danny said they also, for season six, had all of these mini arcs that they were going to add to the season.
丹尼说，他们第六季还有所有这些打算加入到这一季中的迷你剧情线。

95
00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:33.750
Those are little stories that take place over several episodes.
那些是跨越几集的小故事。

96
00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:38.110
And one of those ideas was that Dunder Mifflin was going to go bankrupt.
其中一个想法是邓德·米福林公司要破产了。

97
00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:42.910
And another one was that Jim would get this co-manager position.
另一个是吉姆会得到这个联合经理的职位。

98
00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:43.970
That's already happened.
那已经发生了。

99
00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:52.250
But this episode of the murder mystery game, they thought it tied in really well with that mini arc of Dunder Mifflin going out of business.
但他们认为这一集谋杀之谜游戏与邓德·米福林倒闭的迷你剧情线结合得非常好。

100
00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:53.350
Oh, for sure.
哦，肯定的。

101
00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:56.710
So, there is a DVD commentary for this episode.
这一集有DVD评论音轨。

102
00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:57.270
Oh!
哦！

103
00:04:57.450 --> 00:05:01.410
So, it features Ellie Kemper, Danny Chun, and Greg Daniels.
参与者包括艾丽·坎伯、丹尼·淳和格雷格·丹尼尔斯。

104
00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:05.150
And they talked a little bit about this episode setting up three major arcs.
他们谈到了这一集如何为三个主要剧情线做铺垫。

105
00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:06.450
Like, exactly what you're saying.
就像你刚才说的那样。

106
00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:12.190
The crumbling of Dunder Mifflin, the sail to saber, and Andy and Aaron.
邓德·米夫林的衰落、被赛博收购，以及安迪和艾琳的故事线。

107
00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:14.110
Yes, the Andy and Aaron.
没错，安迪和艾琳的故事线。

108
00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:14.590
You're right.
你说得对。

109
00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:15.470
That's another one.
那也是其中之一。

110
00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:24.950
Danny also told me that the writers played one of these murder mystery games for research in the writer's room.
丹尼还告诉我，编剧们为了找灵感，在编剧室里玩过这种谋杀之谜游戏。

111
00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:29.670
He said they noticed that in all of the games, the people had silly pun names.
他说他们注意到，在所有的游戏里，角色的名字都带有滑稽的双关语。

112
00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:31.650
So, they knew they were going to have to do that.
所以他们知道自己也得这么做。

113
00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:34.930
There was a CD with a narrator that would help you along.
游戏里有一张CD，里面有旁白引导你进行游戏。

114
00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:38.430
He said in the game they played, his character was a Frenchman.
他说在他们玩的那场游戏里，他扮演的是个法国人。

115
00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:43.050
And so, he was stumbling through a French accent while they were playing.
所以他在玩的时候，一直在努力模仿法国口音。

116
00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:47.450
And that kind of gave them the idea that they should have a game where everybody has to have accents.
这让他们产生了一个想法，觉得应该设计一个大家都得用口音说话的游戏。

117
00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:55.010
He also said that they originally thought that this game could be murder in Little Italy.
他还说他们最初想过把游戏背景设定在“小意大利”的谋杀案。

118
00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:58.810
But they were afraid that would feel too much like the Mafia episode.
但他们担心那样会太像《黑手党》那一集了。

119
00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:03.070
And so, that's when they pitched the game Beset in Savannah.
于是，他们提出了“萨凡纳之围”这个游戏主题。

120
00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:09.290
Well, Danny said mainly he just remembered feeling like the game was not that much fun.
丹尼说他主要记得当时觉得这游戏没那么好玩。

121
00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:11.130
It involved a lot of acting.
因为它需要大量的表演。

122
00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:13.710
And so, he thought about that.
所以他思考了一下。

123
00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:19.270
And he thought that's why people like Andy and Michael would like the game.
他觉得这就是为什么像安迪和迈克尔这样的人会喜欢这个游戏。

124
00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:25.130
I just really like how much playing this game in the writer's room informed them.
我真的很喜欢他们在编剧室玩这个游戏的过程，这为他们提供了很多灵感。

125
00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:26.350
You know?
你知道吗？

126
00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:26.910
Yeah.
是的。

127
00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:29.390
Because Danny was like, I don't like playing this game.
因为丹尼当时觉得，我不喜欢玩这个游戏。

128
00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:31.890
I don't like doing an accent and it's too much acting.
我不喜欢模仿口音，这表演成分太多了。

129
00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:35.550
I feel like he now could write very well for Angela.
我觉得他现在能把安吉拉写得很好。

130
00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:36.630
And Stanley.
还有斯坦利。

131
00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:37.050
Yeah.
没错。

132
00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:39.690
But he's like, somebody would like this.
但他觉得，肯定会有人喜欢这个。

133
00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:40.990
I guess Andy and Michael.
我想就是安迪和迈克尔。

134
00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:43.390
I thought this was an amazing episode.
我觉得这一集太棒了。

135
00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:46.510
So, Danny, my gosh, your first one out of the gate.
丹尼，天哪，这是你写的第一集。

136
00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:47.290
Home run.
大获成功。

137
00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:48.650
I really liked it too.
我也非常喜欢。

138
00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:50.050
All right.
好的。

139
00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:53.990
Fast fact number three, Angela, is a fan question from Megan H.
第三个快问快答，安吉拉，是一个来自加拿大艾伯塔省埃德蒙顿的梅根·H提出的粉丝问题。

140
00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:55.950
in Edmonton, Alberta, Canada,
她想知道我们俩是否参加过像剧中那样的谋杀之谜活动。

141
00:06:55.950 --> 00:07:02.430
who would like to know if either of us have ever done a murder mystery event like in the show.
好问题。

142
00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:04.770
Great question.
我确实有个故事。

143
00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:06.610
I actually have a story.
珍娜，你有吗？

144
00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:07.550
Jenna, do you have one?
我也有。

145
00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:08.950
I do too.
好的。

146
00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:09.710
Okay.
你先来。

147
00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:10.890
You go firSt.
哦，好吧。

148
00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:11.390
Oh, okay.
我曾经被邀请参加一个晚宴，他们说会有晚餐，然后我们大家会一起玩一个游戏。

149
00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:16.570
I was once invited to a dinner party where they said there will be dinner and then we will be playing
作为一个团体。

150
00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:18.390
a game as a group.
好的。

151
00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:20.890
Did they say what the game was?
他们说是什么游戏了吗？

152
00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:21.610
No.
没有。

153
00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:22.130
Oh.
噢。

154
00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:27.950
And when I got there at dinner, the host explained the game while we ate our meal.
我到那儿吃晚饭时，主人边吃饭边给我们讲解了游戏规则。

155
00:07:28.230 --> 00:07:29.650
Guess who the hosts were?
猜猜主人是谁？

156
00:07:29.850 --> 00:07:30.350
Who?
谁？

157
00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:32.210
Oscar Nunez.
奥斯卡·努涅斯。

158
00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:32.890
What?
什么？

159
00:07:33.170 --> 00:07:33.510
Yes.
没错。

160
00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:35.030
And his wife, Ursula.
还有他妻子，厄休拉。

161
00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:40.350
Oscar hosted you for a murder mystery game night?
奥斯卡邀请你去参加谋杀之谜游戏之夜？

162
00:07:40.470 --> 00:07:40.830
Yes.
是的。

163
00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:43.170
Was this before this episode or after?
这是在这一集之前还是之后？

164
00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:44.450
Before this episode.
在这一集之前。

165
00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:45.770
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

166
00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.710
So, the game was called Mafia.
那个游戏叫“黑手党”。

167
00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:48.590
Oh, yeah.
噢，对。

168
00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:50.310
This is really a popular game.
这游戏真的很火。

169
00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:50.650
Yes.
是的。

170
00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:53.730
This was like all the rage in Los Angeles for a very long time.
这游戏在洛杉矶风靡了很长一段时间。

171
00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:58.750
I don't know if this went over the whole country, but people were crazy about this game.
我不知道全国是不是都这样，但大家对这游戏简直着了迷。

172
00:07:58.930 --> 00:07:59.830
Crazy about it.
非常着迷。

173
00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:01.150
And they had the rules.
他们有规则说明。

174
00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:03.450
I was actually texting with Ursula yesterday.
我昨天还在和厄休拉发短信。

175
00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:05.050
I was like, Ursula, what did you guys call it?
我问她：厄休拉，你们当时管这叫什么？

176
00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:06.830
Because in my memory, they called it killer.
因为在我的记忆里，他们管这叫“杀手”。

177
00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:08.670
And she goes, no, Angela, it was called Mafia.
她说：不，安吉拉，那叫“黑手党”。

178
00:08:08.870 --> 00:08:09.090
Yes.
没错。

179
00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:12.170
And so, there were about 10 of us at the dinner party.
当时晚宴上大约有10个人。

180
00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:14.610
And there's a few different ways you can play this.
这游戏有几种不同的玩法。

181
00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:21.590
But the way we played it was, there was one mafia, one killer, a detective, a doctor,
但我们的玩法是：有一个黑手党，一个杀手，一个侦探，一个医生，

182
00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:24.290
and a narrator, and then you had the civilians.
还有一个旁白，剩下的人是平民。

183
00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:24.970
Okay.
好的。

184
00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:27.330
And the narrator kind of moves it along.
旁白负责推进游戏进程。

185
00:08:27.510 --> 00:08:30.230
The narrator's who knows who's who, right?
旁白是唯一知道谁是谁的人，对吧？

186
00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:30.990
Oh, okay.
噢，好的。

187
00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:31.710
Because-
因为——

188
00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:34.050
That seems like not as much fun of a part.
那听起来好像没那么好玩。

189
00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:35.350
It actually is.
其实挺好玩的。

190
00:08:35.350 --> 00:08:37.530
I've been the narrator before, and it's kind of fun.
我以前当过旁白，还挺有意思的。

191
00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:38.030
Oh, okay.
噢，好的。

192
00:08:38.130 --> 00:08:38.430
Go ahead.
你继续。

193
00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:42.390
I never played Mafia, which I kind of can't believe, because I'm a sucker for these games.
我从没玩过“黑手党”，简直不敢相信，因为我特别喜欢这类游戏。

194
00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:44.070
I want us to do this.
我想让我们也玩一次。

195
00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:45.170
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

196
00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:46.750
Earwolf Company Party.
Earwolf公司派对。

197
00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:48.890
We play Mafia.
我们玩“黑手党”。

198
00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:50.170
Have you guys played it?
你们玩过吗？

199
00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:51.810
Sam, Cassie, have you played Mafia?
山姆，卡西，你们玩过“黑手党”吗？

200
00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:53.030
No, I haven't.
没有，我没玩过。

201
00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:57.290
But I do remember the absolute stranglehold that it had over everybody for a while.
但我确实记得它曾一度对所有人有着绝对的统治力。

202
00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:57.790
Oh, yeah.
噢，是啊。

203
00:08:58.290 --> 00:09:00.530
Wordle or Animal Crossing at that time.
当时是《Wordle》或者《动物森友会》。

204
00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:00.930
Yes.
没错。

205
00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:01.610
Everybody was in it.
每个人都深陷其中。

206
00:09:01.610 --> 00:09:02.550
Everyone was playing it.
大家都在玩。

207
00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:07.350
So, in Mafia, the game is divided into two phases, day and night.
在“黑手党”游戏中，游戏分为白天和黑夜两个阶段。

208
00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:14.650
During the night, everyone closes their eyes, and the narrator awakens each role.
夜晚时，所有人闭上眼睛，由主持人唤醒每个角色。

209
00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:20.490
So, the narrator starts with the Mafia person, lets them know who it is, because in each round,
主持人先从“黑手党”成员开始，让他们知道自己的身份，因为每一轮

210
00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:21.810
it's someone new, right?
身份都会更换，对吧？

211
00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:27.690
And as the Mafia person, the way you kill someone is you wink at them.
作为“黑手党”，你杀人的方式就是对他们眨眼。

212
00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:29.350
So, you have to be real sneaky.
所以你必须非常隐蔽。

213
00:09:29.570 --> 00:09:30.850
At least that's how we played it.
至少我们是这么玩的。

214
00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:35.050
And then the doctor can choose to save someone or not.
然后医生可以选择是否救人。

215
00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:40.330
And the civilians have to try to figure out, because every time they awaken, someone is
平民则必须设法找出凶手，因为每次他们睁眼时，都有人

216
00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:40.630
dead.
死了。

217
00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:41.550
Oh.
噢。

218
00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:42.090
Right?
对吧？

219
00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:44.510
Because the Mafia person kills someone each time.
因为“黑手党”每次都会杀一个人。

220
00:09:44.510 --> 00:09:48.630
So, the civilians begin questioning each other, and there's a detective role.
所以平民开始互相质问，而且还有一个侦探角色。

221
00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:54.910
But I imagine, though, also, the Mafia person and the doctor, they're pretending, everyone's
但我猜，“黑手党”和医生也在伪装，每个人都在

222
00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:56.150
pretending to be a civilian.
假装自己是平民。

223
00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:56.830
Yes.
是的。

224
00:09:57.010 --> 00:09:57.190
Right.
没错。

225
00:09:57.430 --> 00:09:57.910
Yes.
是的。

226
00:09:58.450 --> 00:09:59.950
And it's so much fun.
而且这真的很有趣。

227
00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:04.050
And one time, I was the Mafia person, and no one figured me out.
有一次我当了“黑手党”，没人发现是我。

228
00:10:04.310 --> 00:10:04.790
Hmm.
嗯。

229
00:10:05.050 --> 00:10:06.250
But what does that say?
但这说明了什么呢？

230
00:10:06.610 --> 00:10:09.050
It says you were very good at pretending to be a civilian.
说明你非常擅长伪装成平民。

231
00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:11.550
You're diabolical.
你真是个恶魔。

232
00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:12.970
It was really, really fun.
那真的、真的很有趣。

233
00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:18.030
But yes, I played a version of this murder mystery with Oscar in real life.
不过没错，我在现实生活中和奥斯卡玩过一个版本的谋杀之谜游戏。

234
00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:18.890
Wow.
哇。

235
00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:20.090
Before this episode.
就在这集节目之前。

236
00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:21.050
Before this episode.
在这集节目之前。

237
00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:22.170
That's very cool.
那太酷了。

238
00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:22.790
I know.
我知道。

239
00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:23.450
Is that crazy?
这不是很疯狂吗？

240
00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:27.190
I did not have to wear a funny hat or have an accent, I should say.
我得说，我没必要戴滑稽的帽子或者装腔作势。

241
00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:29.130
I guess you could have chosen to.
我想你本来是可以选择那样做的。

242
00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:34.890
Well, it is very funny that you say that, Angela, because I did a mini deep dive on the
安吉拉，你说得真有意思，因为我稍微深入研究了一下

243
00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:42.250
murder mystery game genre, and they believe that it began in the first half of the 19th
谋杀之谜游戏类型，他们认为它起源于19世纪上半叶

244
00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:45.270
century with a party game called Wink Murder.
一种叫“眨眼谋杀”的派对游戏。

245
00:10:45.550 --> 00:10:46.010
Oh!
噢！

246
00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:46.850
Yeah.
是啊。

247
00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:52.530
One player is secretly selected as a murderer, and they kill other players by winking at them.
一名玩家被秘密选为凶手，他们通过对其他玩家眨眼来杀人。

248
00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:53.530
That's what we did.
那就是我们玩的那种。

249
00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:57.650
If you get killed, you have to count to five before you die.
如果你被杀了，你得数到五才能“死”。

250
00:10:57.830 --> 00:10:58.230
Yes.
没错。

251
00:10:58.450 --> 00:10:58.830
Right?
对吧？

252
00:10:59.030 --> 00:10:59.210
Yes.
没错。

253
00:10:59.210 --> 00:10:59.670
Is this it?
就是这个吗？

254
00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:04.770
Yes, because you can't just give it away, so you have to, like, make a moment of it.
对，因为你不能直接把它送出去，所以你得，怎么说呢，得营造一种氛围。

255
00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:06.190
This is so weird.
这太奇怪了。

256
00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:08.590
Is Mafia just based on wink murder?
“黑手党”游戏是不是就是基于“眨眼杀人”游戏改编的？

257
00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:10.250
So far, it's sounding like it.
目前听起来确实是这样。

258
00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:11.930
I will say this.
我得说一句。

259
00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:16.470
If you play Mafia with your friends, and you're the murderer, and you're not good at
如果你和朋友玩“黑手党”，而你是杀手，但你又不擅长

260
00:11:16.470 --> 00:11:17.410
winking...
眨眼的话……

261
00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:18.370
Oh, no!
噢，不！

262
00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:20.230
I never thought of that!
我从来没想过这一点！

263
00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:21.470
Like me.
就像我一样。

264
00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:24.090
I think I'm good with one eye.
我觉得我用一只眼睛眨得挺好。

265
00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:26.310
You just winked at me great with both eyes.
你刚才两只眼睛一起眨，眨得可真棒。

266
00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:27.030
Did I really?
真的吗？

267
00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:27.750
Yeah, you did fine.
对，你做得挺好的。

268
00:11:28.050 --> 00:11:28.410
Oh.
噢。

269
00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:30.230
Well, I'm sorry.
好吧，抱歉。

270
00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:32.590
I watched you closer this time.
这次我仔细观察你了。

271
00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:33.450
The right eye.
右眼。

272
00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:37.490
You do regular wink with this eye, and then the other eye, you go...
你用这只眼睛正常眨眼，然后另一只眼睛，你就……

273
00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:38.550
I know.
我知道。

274
00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:45.070
So I can wink in normal speed with one eye, but the other one is like, boonk, boonk.
所以我能用一只眼睛正常速度眨眼，但另一只眼睛就像，砰，砰。

275
00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:45.530
Yeah.
是啊。

276
00:11:45.610 --> 00:11:46.470
Boonk, boonk.
砰，砰。

277
00:11:46.550 --> 00:11:48.290
I can see you concentrating on it.
我能看出你在努力集中注意力。

278
00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:49.070
To try to wink.
试图眨眼。

279
00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:49.430
Yeah.
没错。

280
00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:51.530
So you've got to figure out what's your good eye.
所以你得找出哪只是你的优势眼。

281
00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:54.470
Well, I have never played Mafia.
好吧，我从来没玩过“黑手党”。

282
00:11:54.710 --> 00:11:57.630
I have never played a murder mystery game.
我从来没玩过谋杀悬疑类游戏。

283
00:11:57.770 --> 00:11:58.770
Yeah, what's your story?
是吗，那你有什么故事？

284
00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:00.790
But I was an actor...
但我以前是个演员……

285
00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:01.870
What?
什么？

286
00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:04.310
...in murder mystery dinner theater.
……在谋杀悬疑晚餐剧场里演戏。

287
00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:05.190
Come on!
别逗了！

288
00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:06.050
Yep.
真的。

289
00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:08.090
Is there any footage of that?
有那方面的录像吗？

290
00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:09.630
Can I see any of that?
我能看看吗？

291
00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:14.430
I have a photo of myself in my crushed velvet gown.
我有一张穿着天鹅绒礼服的照片。

292
00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:17.170
I played several parts in several different shows.
我在好几部不同的剧里演过好几个角色。

293
00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:21.550
This was my very first paid live theater acting gig.
那是我第一份有报酬的现场戏剧表演工作。

294
00:12:21.850 --> 00:12:25.130
I did it in St. Louis, Missouri at the Lemp Mansion.
是在密苏里州圣路易斯的兰普大宅做的。

295
00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:26.990
A bunch of people would come in.
当时会有一群人过来。

296
00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:28.530
Wait, was it like an old mansion?
等等，那是那种老宅子吗？

297
00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:31.350
Like a haunted sort of cool like old mansion?
那种闹鬼的、很酷的老宅子？

298
00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:32.170
Yeah.
对。

299
00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:34.370
Yeah, and I even had a ghost encounter there.
没错，我甚至在那里遇到过鬼。

300
00:12:34.510 --> 00:12:34.970
Come on.
别开玩笑了。

301
00:12:34.970 --> 00:12:35.850
While I was working there.
我在那儿工作的时候。

302
00:12:35.890 --> 00:12:36.530
I did.
我真的看到了。

303
00:12:37.070 --> 00:12:37.710
I did.
我确实看到了。

304
00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:39.090
I saw the Lavender Lady.
我看到了薰衣草女士。

305
00:12:39.630 --> 00:12:40.490
Come on.
得了吧。

306
00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:41.230
I did!
我真的看到了！

307
00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:43.210
What is the Lavender Lady?
薰衣草女士是什么？

308
00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:44.090
I don't know.
我不知道。

309
00:12:44.210 --> 00:12:46.470
I didn't know who the Lavender Lady was,
我当时不知道薰衣草女士是谁，

310
00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:50.590
but I was in what was one of the rooms of the house
但我当时就在那栋房子里的一个房间里，

311
00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:53.410
that they designated for the actors to change in.
那是他们指定给演员换装用的房间。

312
00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:53.870
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

313
00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:56.590
And no one was supposed to come in there
而且按理说没人能进来，

314
00:12:56.590 --> 00:12:58.170
because that was our changing room.
因为那是我们的更衣室。

315
00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:01.350
And I heard the door open behind me.
我听到身后的门开了。

316
00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:03.890
And I looked up in the mirror in front of me
我抬头看向面前的镜子，

317
00:13:03.890 --> 00:13:06.130
and behind me by the door, I saw a woman.
在身后门口的位置，我看到了一个女人。

318
00:13:06.350 --> 00:13:08.590
And I said, I'm sorry, you can't be in here.
我说，抱歉，你不能待在这儿。

319
00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:10.610
And when I turned around, there was nothing there.
当我转过身时，那里什么都没有。

320
00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:14.670
So I was fired up.
所以我当时很火大。

321
00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:18.390
I went to the owner of the place and I said,
我去找了那地方的老板，我说，

322
00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:20.170
listen, if you're going to give us a place
听着，如果你要给我们提供一个

323
00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:22.650
to change our clothes, you need to make sure it's secure.
换衣服的地方，你得确保它是安全的。

324
00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:24.790
A woman walked right into that room.
刚才有个女人直接走进了那个房间。

325
00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:27.270
And he said, no one was in that area.
他说，那个区域根本没人。

326
00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:29.690
And I said, well, explain to me how this woman walked in.
我说，那你给我解释一下那个女人是怎么走进去的。

327
00:13:29.770 --> 00:13:31.050
He said, what'd she look like?
他问，她长什么样？

328
00:13:32.150 --> 00:13:35.470
And I said, well, she was, I kind of tried to describe her.
我说，嗯，她……我试着描述了一下她的样子。

329
00:13:35.550 --> 00:13:37.650
I was like, as I was describing her, I realized like,
我当时……就在描述她的时候，我意识到，

330
00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:40.910
I was like, she's wearing a big hat and like a dress.
我当时说，她戴着一顶大帽子，穿着裙子。

331
00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:43.630
And sort of-
还有那种……

332
00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:45.770
I realized I was describing an old timey lady.
我意识到我描述的是一位老派的女士。

333
00:13:46.570 --> 00:13:48.670
And then his face got all white.
然后他的脸刷地一下全白了。

334
00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:51.330
And he was like, oh my gosh, you saw the Lavender Lady.
他说，天哪，你看到了薰衣草女士。

335
00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:52.690
What?
什么？

336
00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:53.370
Yeah.
是的。

337
00:13:53.570 --> 00:13:54.770
I'm out at that point.
那一刻我直接退出了。

338
00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:56.770
I'm, bye-bye, bye dinner theater career.
我直接拜拜了，再见吧，晚餐剧场生涯。

339
00:13:57.090 --> 00:13:57.590
I'm gone.
我走了。

340
00:13:57.810 --> 00:13:59.150
I have to go entertain folks.
我还得去给客人们表演呢。

341
00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.350
They're on their salad course.
他们正在吃沙拉。

342
00:14:00.510 --> 00:14:02.770
I've got to get out there and tell them a murder has happened.
我得赶紧出去告诉他们发生了一起谋杀案。

343
00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:04.130
Wow.
哇。

344
00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:04.850
Yeah.
是啊。

345
00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:07.490
Oh my gosh, that's creepy.
天哪，那太诡异了。

346
00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:08.190
Yeah.
确实。

347
00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:10.510
Wow, you did dinner theater lady.
哇，你居然做过晚餐剧场演员。

348
00:14:10.510 --> 00:14:13.530
You did theater while someone was like buttering a baguette.
你居然在别人抹法棍面包的时候演戏。

349
00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:14.750
Well, here's the thing.
嗯，是这样的。

350
00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:16.010
We did it between courses.
我们是在上菜间隙表演的。

351
00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:17.530
So we'd bring everybody in.
所以我们会把大家都叫进来。

352
00:14:17.610 --> 00:14:18.450
We'd sit them down.
让他们坐下。

353
00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:19.490
They're getting their drinks.
他们正在喝饮料。

354
00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:20.910
We're handing out slips of paper.
我们分发纸条。

355
00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:26.890
It was our job during this mingle to find the people who seemed outgoing enough to play
在这一社交环节，我们的工作是找出那些看起来足够外向的人来扮演

356
00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:27.930
the major roles.
主要角色。

357
00:14:28.110 --> 00:14:29.570
Because you don't want to give-
因为你不想给——

358
00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:30.090
Wait, wait.
等等，等等。

359
00:14:30.150 --> 00:14:32.130
The people eating dinner play a part?
吃晚饭的人也要参与表演？

360
00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:32.770
Oh, yes.
哦，是的。

361
00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:34.170
Everybody gets a part.
每个人都有角色。

362
00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:36.050
Everybody has a funny name.
每个人都有个滑稽的名字。

363
00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:38.270
Someone in the room is the murderer.
房间里有人是凶手。

364
00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:40.090
Oh, I didn't realize that.
哦，我没意识到这一点。

365
00:14:40.170 --> 00:14:45.130
I thought you were performing a murder mystery while people ate dinner and watched you.
我还以为是你们在表演谋杀悬疑剧，而客人们边吃边看。

366
00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:49.750
No, interactive, improvisation slash scripted.
不，是互动式的，即兴加剧本表演。

367
00:14:49.890 --> 00:14:50.910
We had jokes.
我们有笑话。

368
00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:53.610
We had to keep people kind of on the plot.
我们得让人们保持在剧情里。

369
00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:57.190
But, you know, you'd walk people to their table.
但是，你知道，你会领着人们去他们的餐桌。

370
00:14:57.970 --> 00:14:59.110
Waiters giving them a drink.
服务员给他们递上饮料。

371
00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:00.750
You're hobnobbing with them in character.
你以角色的身份与他们寒暄。

372
00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:04.410
And you find the people that seem like they can play the different roles.
然后你找出那些看起来能胜任不同角色的人。

373
00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:06.950
And then you've got these slips of paper and you hand it to them.
接着你拿出这些纸条，递给他们。

374
00:15:06.950 --> 00:15:11.050
And then later you'd be like, where's Bobby Oylton?
之后你会说，鲍比·奥尔顿在哪儿？

375
00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:12.450
Bobby Oylton?
鲍比·奥尔顿？

376
00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:13.070
Oh, yes.
哦，是的。

377
00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:14.950
I saw you when you came in.
你进来的时候我就看见你了。

378
00:15:15.590 --> 00:15:17.930
Bobby, what do you have to say for yourself?
鲍比，你有什么要为自己辩解的吗？

379
00:15:18.050 --> 00:15:21.110
And then he has to read off of his little slip of paper.
然后他就得照着他的小纸条念。

380
00:15:21.410 --> 00:15:22.550
You were Michael Scott.
你当时是迈克尔·斯科特。

381
00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:24.310
Yes, I sort of was.
是的，某种程度上是。

382
00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:25.470
You were Caleb Crawdad.
你当时是凯莱布·克劳达德。

383
00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:27.270
I was sort of Caleb Crawdad.
我某种程度上是凯莱布·克劳达德。

384
00:15:27.390 --> 00:15:27.590
Yeah.
没错。

385
00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:28.710
Wow.
哇。

386
00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:29.550
Yeah.
是啊。

387
00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:32.070
So I did that for two years.
所以我做了两年。

388
00:15:32.810 --> 00:15:34.890
But I got 50 bucks a night.
但我一晚能挣50块钱。

389
00:15:35.130 --> 00:15:39.950
That was, like, good money for acting, for doing what I loved.
对于演戏、做我热爱的事来说，那算是不错的收入了。

390
00:15:40.150 --> 00:15:44.350
I need mom detectives to go to a murder mystery dinner theater.
我需要妈妈侦探们去参加一场谋杀悬疑晚餐剧场。

391
00:15:44.990 --> 00:15:46.450
Put it on a card, Jenna.
记在卡片上，珍娜。

392
00:15:46.730 --> 00:15:49.850
Yeah, we should investigate the Lavender Lady sighting.
没错，我们应该调查一下“薰衣草女士”的目击事件。

393
00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:50.510
Yes!
太棒了！

394
00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:52.510
We'll get to the bottom of it.
我们会查个水落石出。

395
00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:55.110
We will, but we'll have to be in character and wear outfits.
我们会查清楚的，但我们得进入角色并穿上戏服。

396
00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:58.450
Yes, because we'll pretend like we're part of the dinner theater.
没错，因为我们要假装自己是晚餐剧场的一部分。

397
00:15:58.610 --> 00:15:58.890
We're part of the show.
我们是演出的一部分。

398
00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:00.790
My God, it writes itself.
天哪，这剧本简直是自动写好的。

399
00:16:01.510 --> 00:16:02.590
Oh, my God.
哦，天哪。

400
00:16:03.870 --> 00:16:06.550
If I see this on TV one day, I'm going to be so pissed.
如果有一天我在电视上看到这个，我会气疯的。

401
00:16:06.550 --> 00:16:07.370
I'm going to kick someone's ass.
我要去教训某个人。

402
00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:08.590
If it's not you and I.
如果不是你和我。

403
00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:09.590
I know.
我知道。

404
00:16:09.770 --> 00:16:10.570
Kicking some butts.
去教训某个人。

405
00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:11.710
All right.
好吧。

406
00:16:11.810 --> 00:16:13.350
Let's take a break and call our agents.
我们休息一下，给我们的经纪人打个电话。

407
00:16:13.710 --> 00:16:24.780
We are back.
我们回来了。

408
00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:30.040
And today only, Dwight Schrute presents This Year in Martial Arts,
今天，德怀特·舒鲁特将为大家带来《年度武术回顾》，

409
00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:32.660
colon updates, advancements, and et cetera.
包括最新动态、进展等等。

410
00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:35.820
Yes, like Jim said, there's always lots of changes
没错，正如吉姆所说，

411
00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:39.840
to the 1,000-year-old martial arts traditions.
千年武术传统总是在不断演变。

412
00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:42.360
Dwight's going to start with Phyllis.
德怀特要从菲利斯开始。

413
00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:43.900
I clocked some moves.
我记录了一些动作。

414
00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:47.460
Phyllis charges Dwight with what looks to be a two-finger eye jab.
菲利斯向德怀特发起了进攻，看起来像是双指戳眼。

415
00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:48.040
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

416
00:16:48.220 --> 00:16:51.160
Dwight stops her with an arm block that I guess would have broken her arm,
德怀特用手臂格挡住了她，我猜这本该折断她的手臂，

417
00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:52.460
and then he's going to flip her over.
然后他要把她翻过去。

418
00:16:53.020 --> 00:16:53.440
Yeah.
是啊。

419
00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:55.400
He tries to engage Kevin.
他试图向凯文发起挑战。

420
00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:56.480
Kevin's a big no.
凯文果断拒绝了。

421
00:16:56.900 --> 00:16:57.320
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

422
00:16:57.320 --> 00:17:00.720
And all of this is going to lead to Dwight fighting himself.
而这一切最终导致了德怀特与自己对打。

423
00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:01.840
Yes.
没错。

424
00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:05.600
I'd like to point out in this scene at 39 seconds,
我想指出的是，在39秒的这个场景里，

425
00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:08.340
Meredith is wearing the designer sweater vest again.
梅雷迪斯又穿了那件设计师款的毛衣背心。

426
00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:10.020
I clocked that, too.
我也注意到了。

427
00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:13.340
I mean, I feel like this is some sort of personal trolling of me.
我是说，我觉得这简直是在针对我。

428
00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:16.860
Well, I have a few tidbits about this cold open.
好吧，关于这段开场戏，我有一些小道消息。

429
00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:17.920
Oh, really?
哦，真的吗？

430
00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:19.220
I have some as well.
我也有一些。

431
00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:25.940
Well, I'll start by saying we got a lot of mail of people asking if Dwight's self-fight
好吧，我先说，我们收到了很多邮件，人们都在问德怀特的自我对打

432
00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:30.860
was choreographed, and I would like to tell you guys that was all Rainn Wilson.
是不是编排好的，我想告诉大家，那全都是雷恩·威尔逊自己发挥的。

433
00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:32.660
Bravo, Rainn!
干得好，雷恩！

434
00:17:32.720 --> 00:17:33.100
Yes.
没错。

435
00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:37.380
He came up with all of those moves based on descriptions in the script.
他根据剧本里的描述想出了所有那些动作。

436
00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:41.420
We did have our stunt coordinator, Eric Sulke, on board for the day,
我们确实请了特技协调员埃里克·苏尔克在现场待了一天，

437
00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:44.340
just to make sure that Rainn didn't actually hurt himself.
只是为了确保雷恩不会真的伤到自己。

438
00:17:44.340 --> 00:17:49.780
Well, in the DVD commentary, Danny shared that the original version of this cold open
在DVD评论音轨里，丹尼分享说这段开场戏的原始版本

439
00:17:49.780 --> 00:17:53.900
ended with Dwight and Michael kicking each other in the groin.
结尾是德怀特和迈克尔互相踢对方的裆部。

440
00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:54.700
Oh.
哦。

441
00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:55.440
Yeah.
是啊。

442
00:17:55.740 --> 00:18:01.860
But instead, they went with a pitch from Jen Salata, where Dwight fights himself instead.
但后来他们采纳了简·萨拉塔的提议，改成了德怀特与自己对打。

443
00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:05.880
It still ends with Dwight punching himself in the groin,
虽然结尾还是德怀特自己打了自己裆部一拳，

444
00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:11.780
but it was originally scripted to be a self-kick in the groin.
但剧本原本写的是自己踢自己裆部。

445
00:18:12.100 --> 00:18:12.900
It said this.
剧本是这么写的。

446
00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:14.800
How do you kick yourself in the groin?
你怎么能自己踢到自己的裆部呢？

447
00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:16.080
Exactly.
就是说啊。

448
00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:16.540
Yeah.
是啊。

449
00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:18.560
Here's what the script said.
剧本上是这么写的。

450
00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:23.100
Quote, Dwight snaps his leg up and kicks himself in the balls.
引用：德怀特猛地抬腿，踢向自己的蛋蛋。

451
00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:28.600
Dwight's face shows equally the pain of the kick and the pride of winning.
德怀特的脸上既有被踢后的痛苦，也有获胜后的自豪。

452
00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:30.640
That's so great.
太棒了。

453
00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:37.840
On the day, they realized there was no way for Rainn to self-kick himself in the balls,
当时他们意识到，雷恩根本没法自己踢自己的蛋蛋，

454
00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:40.140
that it was just sort of physically impossible.
这在物理上几乎是不可能的。

455
00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:48.060
However, Danny said in an interview that Greg was convinced there was a way to do it.
不过，丹尼在采访中说，格雷格坚信一定有办法做到。

456
00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:57.320
If maybe they could attach a strap to Rainn's leg that would help sort of hoist it up somehow.
比如给雷恩的腿绑上一根带子，想办法把它提起来之类的。

457
00:18:57.400 --> 00:19:03.520
He even sketched it out on the back of his script, which is a very Greg move.
他甚至在剧本背面画了草图，这非常格雷格。

458
00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:08.640
Can't you see Greg turning a script over and like sketching out the self-groin kick strap?
你能想象格雷格翻过剧本，画出那个自踢裆部装置的草图吗？

459
00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:09.980
Here's how it works.
原理是这样的。

460
00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:10.780
Here's the mechanics.
机械结构是这样的。

461
00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:13.160
I want that sketch and I want it in a frame.
我想要那张草图，还要把它裱起来。

462
00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:13.640
Right?
对吧？

463
00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:14.920
Where is that sketch?
那张草图在哪儿呢？

464
00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:18.920
In the end, obviously, this was not happening.
最后，很显然，这事儿没成。

465
00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:21.360
So they had Rainn punch himself in the groin.
所以他们让雷恩自己给了自己裆部一拳。

466
00:19:21.940 --> 00:19:32.860
Greg shared that he really enjoyed directing the cold open and the tag for this episode because they were like mini action movies or the closest thing our show got to little action sequences.
格雷格说他非常喜欢执导这一集的开场戏和结尾彩蛋，因为它们就像迷你动作片，或者说是我们剧里最接近动作戏的部分。

467
00:19:33.180 --> 00:19:34.780
And Jenna, Ellie shared something.
还有珍娜，艾莉分享了一件事。

468
00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:38.860
She said the cold open was filmed the morning of the Emmys.
她说开场戏是在艾美奖颁奖礼那天早上拍的。

469
00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:44.020
Oh, so after Rainn beat himself up, he had to go to the Emmys?
哦，所以雷恩在把自己揍了一顿之后，还得去参加艾美奖？

470
00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:45.120
We all did.
我们都去了。

471
00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:46.340
Wow.
哇。

472
00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:47.360
We worked that day.
我们那天还在工作。

473
00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:54.960
We have shared this before that many times we worked right up until an event and we would have to get ready at the set.
我们之前分享过，很多时候我们工作到活动开始前一刻，还得在片场准备。

474
00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:55.620
Yeah.
没错。

475
00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:58.600
And the Emmys were traditionally on a Monday night.
而且艾美奖传统上是在周一晚上举行。

476
00:19:58.880 --> 00:19:59.220
Yeah.
是的。

477
00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:03.420
Which was rough because it would be like the beginning of your work week.
这很辛苦，因为那通常是一周工作的开始。

478
00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:06.400
Oh, and you'd be wrecked for the whole rest of the week.
哦，那你接下来的一整周都会累垮的。

479
00:20:06.960 --> 00:20:07.480
Wow.
哇。

480
00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:10.180
We worked this day and then we went to the Emmys.
我们那天工作完就直接去了艾美奖。

481
00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:12.360
Oh, one last thing.
哦，最后还有一件事。

482
00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:14.840
I have a Dwight flyer count.
我统计了一下德怀特的传单数量。

483
00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:15.640
Oh.
哦。

484
00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:20.300
Because clearly you need to have multiple flyers for your year-end martial art update.
因为显然，你的年终武术更新需要多张传单才行。

485
00:20:20.560 --> 00:20:20.920
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

486
00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:26.780
We have one on each of Jim's glass walls and we have one on the door by accounting.
吉姆的玻璃墙上各有一张，会计部旁边的门上也有一张。

487
00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:29.580
Three in view during the whole cold open.
整个开场戏里能看到三张。

488
00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:31.140
I don't know about the rest of the bullpen.
不知道办公区其他地方还有没有。

489
00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:32.340
Or the kitchen.
或者厨房里。

490
00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:33.320
Or the break room.
或者休息室里。

491
00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:33.920
I know.
我知道。

492
00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:35.020
I'm sure they're everywhere.
我敢肯定到处都是。

493
00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:39.340
They're not there for the rest of the episode, but there's three visible for the cold open.
这一集剩下的部分里它们就不见了，但在开场戏里能看到三张。

494
00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:41.500
Well, now we're going to get into this episode.
好了，现在我们要进入这一集的内容了。

495
00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:48.740
It opens with some weird banter between Michael and Andy about sculpting stand-up comedy.
开场是迈克尔和安迪之间关于雕塑单口喜剧的奇怪闲聊。

496
00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:52.840
And it's interrupted by Dwight receiving an email.
然后被德怀特收到的一封邮件打断了。

497
00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:55.380
And Michael's like, you need to be more specific.
迈克尔说，你需要说得更具体一点。

498
00:20:55.380 --> 00:20:57.280
I get like eight emails a day.
我一天大概能收到八封邮件。

499
00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:58.100
Eight, Jenna.
八封，珍娜。

500
00:20:58.480 --> 00:20:59.620
He gets eight.
他收到了八封。

501
00:20:59.920 --> 00:21:05.760
It's really weird that before we started recording today, we were discussing our email inboxes.
真奇怪，今天录音开始前，我们竟然在讨论各自的电子邮箱收件箱。

502
00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:06.700
Yeah.
是啊。

503
00:21:06.940 --> 00:21:10.480
So, guys, Sam and Jenna are really tidy about their email inbox.
所以，各位，Sam和Jenna在整理收件箱这方面真的很整洁。

504
00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:18.160
Like, they get to zero and then they ask me what my inbox said and my inbox says 1,582.
比如，他们能清空到零，然后问我的收件箱有多少，我的显示是1582封。

505
00:21:18.820 --> 00:21:22.420
And Sam and I are still processing that and we're –
Sam和我还在消化这个事实，我们……

506
00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:24.580
It gave you like hives for a minute.
你当时简直都要起荨麻疹了。

507
00:21:24.660 --> 00:21:25.900
Yeah, we're having a hard time.
没错，我们很难接受。

508
00:21:26.060 --> 00:21:27.620
I don't mean this as an attack.
我不是要攻击你。

509
00:21:27.820 --> 00:21:28.080
Uh-oh.
噢，糟了。

510
00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:29.520
But the way you live is chaos.
但你的生活方式简直是一团糟。

511
00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:34.260
Sam's at zero right now.
Sam现在是零封。

512
00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:36.560
I'm at 10 unread emails.
我有10封未读邮件。

513
00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:42.040
Actually, do you remember in the break, there was a great Jenna moment where you were looking for an email and you couldn't find it.
说真的，还记得休息的时候吗？Jenna有个很棒的瞬间，当时你在找一封邮件，结果没找到。

514
00:21:42.100 --> 00:21:43.660
And Jenna goes, oh, I'm sorry, can you not?
然后Jenna说，噢，抱歉，你能别这样吗？

515
00:21:44.220 --> 00:21:44.520
Yeah.
是啊。

516
00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:47.100
I was like, oh, you can't find the email I sent you?
我当时心想，噢，你找不到我发给你的邮件？

517
00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:50.040
I think I sent it on Monday or Tuesday.
我想我是周一或周二发的。

518
00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:55.600
Well, I got a few emails since I last checked and now I'm 1,583.
好吧，我上次查看之后又收到了几封，现在我有1583封了。

519
00:21:56.300 --> 00:22:06.600
See, you do what Lee does, which is if you can tell that it's something you don't need to read, like it's, I don't know, an ad or something, you don't delete it.
你看，你和Lee的做法一样，如果你看出那是不需要读的内容，比如什么广告之类的，你也不会删掉。

520
00:22:06.700 --> 00:22:07.560
You just skip it.
你只是跳过它。

521
00:22:07.740 --> 00:22:09.300
And then it stays unread.
然后它就一直处于未读状态。

522
00:22:09.540 --> 00:22:09.880
Yes.
没错。

523
00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:11.280
I delete those.
我会把那些删掉。

524
00:22:11.520 --> 00:22:13.260
I don't want that cluttering me.
我不想让它们弄乱我的收件箱。

525
00:22:13.260 --> 00:22:14.600
No, you do it right.
不，你做得对。

526
00:22:14.920 --> 00:22:16.440
That's the way you should do it.
那才是你应该做的方式。

527
00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:18.940
But if it doesn't bother you, then you're not doing it wrong.
但如果那不困扰你，那你也没做错。

528
00:22:18.940 --> 00:22:21.060
It would bother me if I did it your way.
如果我用你的那种方式，我会被困扰的。

529
00:22:22.200 --> 00:22:25.600
Well, Michael only gets eight, so I guess he's not super stressed out.
好吧，Michael只有八封，我想他应该没那么大压力。

530
00:22:26.120 --> 00:22:27.220
I guess he's not.
我想他确实没有。

531
00:22:28.160 --> 00:22:34.620
The email that Dwight is talking about is from David Wallace, and it is referring to an article in the journal.
Dwight提到的那封邮件来自David Wallace，指的是期刊上的一篇文章。

532
00:22:35.240 --> 00:22:36.420
I mean, the wall.
我是说，那堵“墙”。

533
00:22:36.860 --> 00:22:37.300
Yeah.
是啊。

534
00:22:37.580 --> 00:22:38.740
As Michael calls it.
正如Michael所称呼的那样。

535
00:22:38.740 --> 00:22:40.080
Yeah, oh, the wall, right?
对，噢，那堵“墙”，对吧？

536
00:22:40.720 --> 00:22:47.420
Oscar finds the article, but in order to read it, you have to pay an extra $1.99 to get past the paywall.
Oscar找到了那篇文章，但为了阅读它，你必须额外支付1.99美元才能越过付费墙。

537
00:22:48.040 --> 00:22:55.100
Danny shared that they spent like five hours researching the rules of the Wall Street Journal's paywall at that time.
Danny分享说，他们当时花了大概五个小时研究《华尔街日报》付费墙的规则。

538
00:22:55.500 --> 00:23:02.060
He said, apparently, if you're referencing a specific publication, you cannot make up a fact like that that's not true.
他说，显然，如果你引用特定的出版物，你就不能编造那种不属实的事实。

539
00:23:02.060 --> 00:23:06.040
Oh, so at that time, that was the rule?
噢，所以当时那是规则？

540
00:23:06.220 --> 00:23:07.080
Of the paywall.
关于付费墙的规则。

541
00:23:07.540 --> 00:23:07.960
Interesting.
有意思。

542
00:23:07.980 --> 00:23:10.800
Why did it take five hours to get that information?
为什么获取那个信息要花五个小时？

543
00:23:11.140 --> 00:23:15.380
I think they just had to get it correctly, and Jenna, they didn't have the Google back then.
我想他们只是必须确保准确，而且Jenna，那时候他们还没有谷歌呢。

544
00:23:15.680 --> 00:23:17.760
They had Google back then?
那时候他们有谷歌吗？

545
00:23:17.760 --> 00:23:19.440
It was like 2009.
那时大概是2009年。

546
00:23:20.100 --> 00:23:22.000
They didn't have the same search engines we had.
他们没有我们现在用的那种搜索引擎。

547
00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:23.140
Yeah, 100% they did.
不，百分之百是有谷歌的。

548
00:23:24.600 --> 00:23:27.180
How old do you think Google is?
你觉得谷歌有多老了？

549
00:23:27.520 --> 00:23:28.380
It's new.
它是新的。

550
00:23:28.600 --> 00:23:29.700
Google is new.
谷歌是新的。

551
00:23:29.760 --> 00:23:32.400
I'm going to Google, when did Google start?
我要去查一下谷歌，谷歌是什么时候成立的？

552
00:23:32.840 --> 00:23:37.620
Well, I don't know why it took them five hours, but that's what he said on the DVD commentary.
好吧，我不知道为什么他们花了五个小时，但DVD评论里他是这么说的。

553
00:23:37.900 --> 00:23:39.520
They had to be thorough, Jenna.
他们必须得彻底搞清楚，珍娜。

554
00:23:40.100 --> 00:23:42.880
What were you Googling in 2009?
你在2009年的时候在谷歌上搜什么？

555
00:23:43.360 --> 00:23:44.600
Don't put this on us.
别把这事赖在我们头上。

556
00:23:44.740 --> 00:23:45.200
Any number.
随便哪个数字都行。

557
00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:46.740
I'm not saying you.
我不是在说你。

558
00:23:46.880 --> 00:23:49.180
I'm saying people listening.
我是在说听众们。

559
00:23:49.960 --> 00:23:50.660
Hold on.
等等。

560
00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:52.660
What did you Google in 2009?
你在2009年搜了什么？

561
00:23:53.140 --> 00:23:56.240
Google started September 4th, 1998.
谷歌成立于1998年9月4日。

562
00:23:56.700 --> 00:23:58.300
But their search engine.
但他们的搜索引擎呢。

563
00:23:58.420 --> 00:24:00.060
I'm going to get more specific.
我要查得更具体一点。

564
00:24:00.440 --> 00:24:00.500
Thank you.
谢谢。

565
00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:05.060
When did the Google search engine really come into effect?
谷歌搜索引擎到底是什么时候真正投入使用的？

566
00:24:05.300 --> 00:24:07.040
Not really come into effect.
不是真正投入使用。

567
00:24:07.040 --> 00:24:10.480
When did people start using the Google search engine?
人们是从什么时候开始使用谷歌搜索引擎的？

568
00:24:11.300 --> 00:24:11.940
1998!
1998年！

569
00:24:12.460 --> 00:24:14.460
And it really became popular around 2000.
而且它大约在2000年左右真正流行起来。

570
00:24:14.820 --> 00:24:15.820
Thank you, Sam!
谢谢你，萨姆！

571
00:24:15.820 --> 00:24:16.880
I don't believe it.
我不信。

572
00:24:17.140 --> 00:24:20.020
No one was Googling until like two years ago.
直到两年前左右才有人开始用谷歌搜索。

573
00:24:26.140 --> 00:24:29.740
Okay, everyone, Angela discovered Google a couple of years ago.
好了，各位，安吉拉是几年前才发现谷歌的。

574
00:24:29.900 --> 00:24:35.020
Listen, I don't know why it took them five hours, but they clearly had to get it right.
听着，我不知道为什么他们花了五个小时，但他们显然必须得把它弄对。

575
00:24:35.380 --> 00:24:37.040
Maybe they had to get on the phone with someone.
也许他们得跟某人通个电话。

576
00:24:37.180 --> 00:24:38.660
I'm not judging our writers, Jenna.
我不是在评判我们的编剧，珍娜。

577
00:24:38.940 --> 00:24:40.620
I just thought it was a long time.
我只是觉得那时间太长了。

578
00:24:40.820 --> 00:24:42.540
Well, Jenna's judging you guys.
好吧，是珍娜在评判你们。

579
00:24:42.540 --> 00:24:44.780
Here's what I want to point out about this scene.
关于这场戏，我想指出一点。

580
00:24:44.960 --> 00:24:55.440
As we're all gathered around the computer and everybody's reading this article off of Oscar's computer, we're learning that Dunder Mifflin might be, I guess, going into debt,
当我们都围在电脑前，大家都在读奥斯卡电脑上的那篇文章时，我们了解到邓德·米夫林公司可能，我想，正陷入债务危机，

581
00:24:55.600 --> 00:24:57.340
going under, filing for bankruptcy.
濒临倒闭，申请破产。

582
00:24:57.540 --> 00:24:57.680
Yeah.
没错。

583
00:24:58.420 --> 00:25:02.720
Angela, this entire scene, you are blocking me.
安吉拉，整场戏你都在挡着我。

584
00:25:03.160 --> 00:25:07.440
You cannot see my face in this scene because you are standing directly in front of me.
在这场戏里你根本看不到我的脸，因为你就直接站在我前面。

585
00:25:07.600 --> 00:25:12.080
And then finally, you move out of the way and John blocks me.
然后最后，你走开了，约翰又挡住了我。

586
00:25:12.420 --> 00:25:13.580
Did you take a picture?
你拍照了吗？

587
00:25:13.940 --> 00:25:14.640
Yes, I did.
拍了。

588
00:25:14.660 --> 00:25:19.100
It was so funny to me because one of you is blocking me the whole time.
我觉得太搞笑了，因为你们俩一直轮流挡着我。

589
00:25:19.100 --> 00:25:23.160
We talked that morning and we were like, today is the day, John.
那天早上我们商量过，我们当时说，就是今天，约翰。

590
00:25:23.480 --> 00:25:29.380
You and I, I'm going to wear my three-inch heels and I'm going to make sure I block that shot.
你和我，我要穿上我的三英寸高跟鞋，确保我能挡住那个镜头。

591
00:25:29.540 --> 00:25:31.120
Here, I put them all together.
给你，我把它们都拼在一起了。

592
00:25:31.840 --> 00:25:33.060
We really are.
我们确实是故意的。

593
00:25:33.440 --> 00:25:35.060
Why didn't anyone say anything?
为什么当时没人说点什么？

594
00:25:35.320 --> 00:25:36.060
I don't know.
我不知道。

595
00:25:36.700 --> 00:25:41.360
So we don't know how Pam feels about this article because we can never see her.
所以我们不知道帕姆对这篇文章有什么感觉，因为我们根本看不到她。

596
00:25:41.520 --> 00:25:41.800
You can't see her face.
你根本看不到她的脸。

597
00:25:42.660 --> 00:25:43.180
Sorry.
抱歉。

598
00:25:46.200 --> 00:25:48.580
I rarely was able to block anyone.
我很少有机会能挡住别人。

599
00:25:49.100 --> 00:25:50.680
It's a personal victory, I guess.
我想这算是一次个人胜利吧。

600
00:25:50.880 --> 00:25:51.160
I know.
我知道。

601
00:25:51.780 --> 00:25:54.680
Well, what's funny is they all stop at the $1.99.
有趣的是，他们都停在了1.99美元那里。

602
00:25:54.920 --> 00:25:58.060
They're like, oh, I guess we're not going to know what really happens with the company.
他们就像是，哦，看来我们没法知道公司到底发生了什么。

603
00:25:58.280 --> 00:25:59.960
And then Jim enters in his information.
然后吉姆输入了他的信息。

604
00:26:00.400 --> 00:26:00.760
Yes.
没错。

605
00:26:00.980 --> 00:26:04.800
This sends Michael on a spiral and he calls David Wallace.
这让迈克尔陷入了崩溃，他给大卫·华莱士打了电话。

606
00:26:05.080 --> 00:26:06.340
But David's in a meeting.
但大卫正在开会。

607
00:26:07.100 --> 00:26:09.860
I was curious about two moments in this scene.
我对这一幕里的两个时刻很好奇。

608
00:26:10.260 --> 00:26:10.720
Okay.
好的。

609
00:26:11.200 --> 00:26:14.920
One was I was wondering if Steve improvised the way he said,
一个是我想知道史蒂夫说那句台词的方式是不是即兴的，

610
00:26:15.080 --> 00:26:16.480
you should spy on him.
你应该监视他。

611
00:26:16.620 --> 00:26:18.080
Wouldn't that be so hilarious?
那不是很搞笑吗？

612
00:26:19.100 --> 00:26:19.480
Okay.
好的。

613
00:26:20.280 --> 00:26:22.820
I was like, did they tell Steve to say it like that?
我在想，是不是他们让史蒂夫那样说的？

614
00:26:22.980 --> 00:26:24.080
I went to the script.
我查了剧本。

615
00:26:24.280 --> 00:26:28.220
And it said on that line, in parentheses, Valley Girl.
那行台词的括号里写着：山谷女孩腔。

616
00:26:28.560 --> 00:26:29.540
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

617
00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:33.040
So they did give him sort of a line read.
所以他们确实给了他某种台词指导。

618
00:26:33.220 --> 00:26:33.680
Yes.
是的。

619
00:26:33.980 --> 00:26:37.760
The other thing I was curious about was the line in the script when Michael says,
我好奇的另一件事是剧本里迈克尔说的那句台词，

620
00:26:37.860 --> 00:26:39.080
catch you on the flippity flip.
回头再聊。

621
00:26:39.440 --> 00:26:39.820
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

622
00:26:39.820 --> 00:26:41.960
I was like, that sounds like something Steve would improvise.
我当时想，这听起来像是史蒂夫会即兴发挥的东西。

623
00:26:42.320 --> 00:26:42.800
No.
不是。

624
00:26:43.040 --> 00:26:45.180
So that line was in the script, too.
所以那句台词也在剧本里。

625
00:26:45.380 --> 00:26:51.200
And Danny shared on the DVD commentary that Gene Stepnitsky actually pitched catch you
丹尼在DVD评论音轨里分享说，吉恩·斯泰普尼茨基其实在另一集里提议过用

626
00:26:51.200 --> 00:26:53.480
on the flippity flip for a different episode.
回头再聊这句台词。

627
00:26:53.480 --> 00:26:56.240
And the writers loved it, but it didn't make it in.
编剧们很喜欢，但没能用上。

628
00:26:56.340 --> 00:26:58.120
So they kept trying to get this line in.
所以他们一直想把这句台词塞进去。

629
00:26:58.260 --> 00:26:59.120
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

630
00:26:59.480 --> 00:27:00.200
Episode after episode.
一集又一集。

631
00:27:00.440 --> 00:27:01.660
And they finally got it in.
最后他们终于把它加进去了。

632
00:27:01.660 --> 00:27:05.500
Well, you know when Michael goes to the bathroom and he's been vomiting, but then he tries
你知道迈克尔去洗手间呕吐，但后来他试图

633
00:27:05.500 --> 00:27:09.080
to tell Kevin he was just pooping.
告诉凯文他只是在拉屎。

634
00:27:09.420 --> 00:27:11.440
We had a fan question from Kelly C.
我们收到了来自密歇根州凯莉·C的一位粉丝提问。

635
00:27:11.520 --> 00:27:11.920
in Michigan.
是谁写了那句“只是拉屎，你知道我这人就这样”？

636
00:27:11.980 --> 00:27:14.800
Who wrote the line, just pooping, you know how I be?
是丹尼写的。

637
00:27:15.500 --> 00:27:16.380
That was Danny.
丹尼说这是他最引以为傲的台词之一。

638
00:27:17.340 --> 00:27:19.640
Danny said it's one of the lines he's most proud of.
那确实是一句很棒的台词。

639
00:27:19.880 --> 00:27:21.060
It's a great line.
哦，安吉拉，我还想再说一件事。

640
00:27:21.580 --> 00:27:24.040
Oh, I also wanted to say one more thing, Angela.
回到办公室，当迈克尔打电话试图联系大卫·华莱士时，

641
00:27:24.600 --> 00:27:29.080
Back in the office when Michael calls and tries to get in touch with David Wallace, once
我们再次请到了苏珊娜·沃森为大卫的助理斯蒂芬妮配音，她

642
00:27:29.080 --> 00:27:33.560
again, we had Suzanne Watson as the voice of David's assistant, Stephanie, and she's
一直都很棒。

643
00:27:33.560 --> 00:27:34.140
always great.
太棒了。

644
00:27:34.340 --> 00:27:34.860
So great.
所以在剧本里，珍娜，他们增加了更多场景来展示迈克尔真的崩溃了。

645
00:27:35.460 --> 00:27:41.180
So in the script, Jenna, they built in more scenes to show Michael really spiraling.
你知道，他给大卫打电话，在洗手间呕吐。

646
00:27:41.360 --> 00:27:44.120
You know, he calls David, he vomits in the bathroom.
他还开始在艾琳的前台前踱步，等着电话，等着

647
00:27:44.440 --> 00:27:50.320
He also just starts pacing in front of Aaron's reception, waiting for the phone call, waiting
看她是否会示意有人打进来了。

648
00:27:50.320 --> 00:27:52.720
to see if she signals him that someone's calling.
这太搞笑了。

649
00:27:53.340 --> 00:27:54.280
It's so funny.
我想放给你听听。

650
00:27:54.500 --> 00:27:55.760
I want to play it for you.
我想放给你听听。

651
00:27:56.040 --> 00:27:57.060
It's in the deleted scenes.
那在删减片段里。

652
00:27:57.220 --> 00:27:59.320
The first part I'm calling, Michael is pissed.
第一部分我称之为“迈克尔很火大”。

653
00:28:00.960 --> 00:28:03.280
If it's not for me, don't make it look like it's for me, okay?
如果不是给我的，就别搞得好像是给我的，好吗？

654
00:28:03.280 --> 00:28:03.920
I'm sorry.
对不起。

655
00:28:04.160 --> 00:28:05.680
Because I'm going to s*** my pants.
因为我快要吓尿了。

656
00:28:05.740 --> 00:28:06.300
Okay, I'm sorry.
行，对不起。

657
00:28:06.480 --> 00:28:07.060
It's my fault.
是我的错。

658
00:28:13.180 --> 00:28:16.020
Michael, I'm sorry before that I did not know what you were talking about.
迈克尔，我很抱歉之前不知道你在说什么。

659
00:28:16.760 --> 00:28:17.480
Don't, okay.
别说了，好吗。

660
00:28:18.940 --> 00:28:19.660
Do you want anything for-
你想要什么……

661
00:28:19.660 --> 00:28:20.300
Don't even talk.
别说话。

662
00:28:20.440 --> 00:28:21.280
Don't even talk to me.
别跟我说话。

663
00:28:21.520 --> 00:28:21.880
Okay.
好吧。

664
00:28:22.600 --> 00:28:23.080
All right.
行吧。

665
00:28:23.080 --> 00:28:24.420
If they do call, don't-
如果他们真的打电话来，别……

666
00:28:24.420 --> 00:28:26.260
Only if they call me, then talk to me, okay?
只有他们打给我时，你再跟我说，好吗？

667
00:28:26.520 --> 00:28:31.360
If it's anything else, or if you want to apologize to me for calling me when they weren't calling,
如果是其他事，或者如果你想因为在他们没打电话时打扰我而道歉，

668
00:28:32.080 --> 00:28:33.720
then don't do that, all right?
那就别做了，好吗？

669
00:28:33.880 --> 00:28:34.480
Do you understand?
你明白吗？

670
00:28:35.760 --> 00:28:40.240
You're very, very nice, but you're really, you're kind of pissing me off, okay?
你人真的很好，但你真的，你有点惹火我了，好吗？

671
00:28:40.340 --> 00:28:40.520
Sorry.
抱歉。

672
00:28:45.000 --> 00:28:45.380
No.
不。

673
00:28:45.960 --> 00:28:46.960
I thought she lied.
我以为她在撒谎。

674
00:28:47.140 --> 00:28:48.000
I thought she said sorry.
我以为她说对不起。

675
00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:54.960
So, her sorry looks like she's about to laugh, but then she turns it into like a cry, and
所以，她的道歉看起来像是要笑出来，但随后又转成了哭腔，而且

676
00:28:54.960 --> 00:28:59.340
then poor Erin, she's so confused by Michael, it continues, and you've got to hear it.
可怜的艾琳被迈克尔搞糊涂了，事情还在继续，你一定要听听看。

677
00:29:01.160 --> 00:29:02.320
Don't cry, don't cry, please.
别哭，别哭，求你了。

678
00:29:02.640 --> 00:29:03.240
Don't cry.
别哭。

679
00:29:03.860 --> 00:29:07.260
Everybody's sort of high-strung, so chalk it up to that.
大家都有点神经紧绷，所以归咎于这个吧。

680
00:29:09.440 --> 00:29:10.340
We're all in it together.
我们都在同一条船上。

681
00:29:10.580 --> 00:29:11.000
Well, don't laugh either.
嗯，也别笑。

682
00:29:11.180 --> 00:29:12.280
Just don't cry and don't laugh.
就是别哭也别笑。

683
00:29:12.420 --> 00:29:12.740
Good?
行吗？

684
00:29:12.980 --> 00:29:13.300
All right.
好吧。

685
00:29:15.760 --> 00:29:17.380
It's such a funny moment.
那真是一个有趣的时刻。

686
00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:19.160
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

687
00:29:19.300 --> 00:29:21.500
I love the dynamic between those two.
我喜欢他们两人之间的互动。

688
00:29:21.600 --> 00:29:25.380
They really did a good job of creating a different dynamic than what Pam and Michael had.
他们确实做得很好，创造出了一种与帕姆和迈克尔完全不同的互动模式。

689
00:29:25.560 --> 00:29:26.640
Yeah, I mean, Michael.
是啊，我是说，迈克尔。

690
00:29:26.640 --> 00:29:28.400
She so earnestly wants to help him.
她非常真诚地想要帮助他。

691
00:29:28.600 --> 00:29:31.360
She so earnestly wants to be liked by him.
她非常真诚地想要得到他的喜爱。

692
00:29:31.460 --> 00:29:31.680
Yeah.
是啊。

693
00:29:31.860 --> 00:29:33.640
And Michael with Pam, it's the reverse.
而迈克尔和帕姆之间，情况正好相反。

694
00:29:33.640 --> 00:29:35.660
Michael wants to be in Pam's life.
迈克尔想要介入帕姆的生活。

695
00:29:35.840 --> 00:29:36.180
Yes.
没错。

696
00:29:37.080 --> 00:29:37.520
Ugh.
呃。

697
00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:44.300
Well, instead of all that, he's going to go into his office and play the Sean Mullen song,
好吧，与其纠结那些，他打算回办公室去放肖恩·穆伦的那首歌，

698
00:29:44.300 --> 00:29:50.480
Lullaby, I found out from Randy Cordray that it cost us $45,000 to have this song in the
《摇篮曲》，我从兰迪·科德雷那里得知，为了在剧中加入这首歌，

699
00:29:50.480 --> 00:29:51.860
show, to have this clip.
为了这段片段，我们花了45,000美元。

700
00:29:52.400 --> 00:29:52.760
Hmm.
嗯。

701
00:29:53.320 --> 00:29:55.160
Well, I have a background catch.
好吧，我有个背景花絮。

702
00:29:55.320 --> 00:30:00.760
At 5 minutes, 29 seconds, Michael says he needs more Mullins, and he hits the volume
在5分29秒，迈克尔说他需要更多马林斯，然后他反复按下了键盘上的音量键。

703
00:30:00.760 --> 00:30:02.180
button on his keyboard repeatedly.
好的。

704
00:30:02.480 --> 00:30:02.700
Okay.
好吧。

705
00:30:03.300 --> 00:30:08.080
Greg shared that they worked really hard in editing to get that sound to match Steve hitting
格雷格分享说，他们在剪辑时非常努力，才让那个声音和史蒂夫敲击键盘的动作对上。

706
00:30:08.080 --> 00:30:08.740
the keyboard.
键盘。

707
00:30:08.740 --> 00:30:14.400
And Danny shared that after the episode aired, the comment boards were full of people saying
丹尼还说，在那集播出后，评论区里全是人说那是苹果电脑的声音，而迈克尔用的是个人电脑。

708
00:30:14.400 --> 00:30:18.160
that that was a Mac sound, and Michael is using a PC.
那是个苹果电脑的声音，而迈克尔用的是个人电脑。

709
00:30:18.660 --> 00:30:20.200
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

710
00:30:20.380 --> 00:30:21.120
Is that funny?
这很有趣吗？

711
00:30:21.640 --> 00:30:22.200
Yes.
是的。

712
00:30:22.880 --> 00:30:23.860
Oh, wow.
哇哦。

713
00:30:23.860 --> 00:30:26.640
They picked the wrong volume up sound.
他们选错了音量调节的声音。

714
00:30:27.200 --> 00:30:29.920
Well, Jim's going to come in during all of this.
好吧，吉姆会在这一切发生时走进来。

715
00:30:30.340 --> 00:30:32.780
He's like, Michael, you have to pull it together.
他就像是说，迈克尔，你得振作起来。

716
00:30:33.100 --> 00:30:37.260
Like, basically, he's saying you're our leader, and if you're freaking out, it's freaking out
基本上，他是在说你是我们的领导，如果你惊慌失措，大家也都会跟着慌，我们需要让这一天恢复正常。

717
00:30:37.260 --> 00:30:39.880
everyone, we need to just make this a normal day.
大家也都会跟着慌，我们需要让这一天恢复正常。

718
00:30:40.060 --> 00:30:40.840
What's on the agenda?
议程上有什么？

719
00:30:41.320 --> 00:30:43.640
Michael's like, well, we're supposed to have a staff meeting.
迈克尔说，好吧，我们本来应该开个员工会议的。

720
00:30:43.840 --> 00:30:45.220
And Jim's like, great.
吉姆说，太好了。

721
00:30:45.420 --> 00:30:45.760
Right.
没错。

722
00:30:45.980 --> 00:30:47.420
Everyone in the conference room.
所有人去会议室。

723
00:30:47.640 --> 00:30:50.760
Have we ever seen Jim so excited to go into the conference room before?
我们以前见过吉姆这么兴奋地去会议室吗？

724
00:30:51.400 --> 00:30:54.300
No, but he says he only slacks off when things are good.
没有，但他确实说过他只有在一切顺利时才会偷懒。

725
00:30:54.300 --> 00:30:59.600
So I guess, you know, when the s**t hits the fan, he becomes very professional.
所以我猜，当麻烦来临时，他变得非常专业。

726
00:30:59.840 --> 00:31:05.300
It's so funny because I feel like people would be equally freaked out by Jim suddenly having
这太搞笑了，因为我觉得如果吉姆突然有了职业道德，大家也会同样感到惊慌。

727
00:31:05.300 --> 00:31:06.120
a work ethic.
一个职业道德。

728
00:31:06.120 --> 00:31:08.140
They'd be like, uh-oh, uh-oh.
他们会觉得，噢，糟糕，噢，糟糕。

729
00:31:08.380 --> 00:31:08.900
What's happening?
发生什么事了？

730
00:31:09.120 --> 00:31:10.000
Stuff is bad.
情况不妙。

731
00:31:10.200 --> 00:31:11.240
Jim wants to work.
吉姆想工作了。

732
00:31:11.460 --> 00:31:11.640
Yeah.
是啊。

733
00:31:12.180 --> 00:31:13.180
Mom is getting serious.
妈妈要认真起来了。

734
00:31:13.180 --> 00:31:14.000
What's going on?
怎么回事？

735
00:31:14.140 --> 00:31:14.600
Exactly.
没错。

736
00:31:15.460 --> 00:31:18.920
In the conference room, Jim addresses the group.
在会议室里，吉姆向大家讲话。

737
00:31:19.340 --> 00:31:22.880
At 5 minutes 56 seconds, Ryan is wearing glasses.
在5分56秒，瑞安戴着眼镜。

738
00:31:23.460 --> 00:31:24.780
That was my big takeaway.
这是我最大的发现。

739
00:31:25.340 --> 00:31:30.120
Ryan is wearing glasses, and everyone's in the conference room but Kelly.
瑞安戴着眼镜，除了凯莉，所有人都到了会议室。

740
00:31:30.760 --> 00:31:31.620
Where's Kelly?
凯莉在哪？

741
00:31:31.880 --> 00:31:32.860
Where is Kelly?
凯莉在哪？

742
00:31:32.860 --> 00:31:36.580
Kelly, let me tell you, she's only in one scene this entire episode.
凯莉，我告诉你，她整集只出现了一个镜头。

743
00:31:36.760 --> 00:31:37.800
What was she doing?
她在干什么？

744
00:31:38.160 --> 00:31:39.320
Where was Mindy?
明迪去哪了？

745
00:31:39.520 --> 00:31:40.400
I don't know.
我不知道。

746
00:31:41.080 --> 00:31:44.480
Michael has to leave the conference room to take a phone call.
迈克尔不得不离开会议室去接个电话。

747
00:31:44.760 --> 00:31:47.640
And Dwight has one of my favorite lines in the episode.
德怀特说了这集里我最喜欢的台词之一。

748
00:31:47.960 --> 00:31:48.700
What is it?
是什么？

749
00:31:48.860 --> 00:31:50.620
He says, he needs me.
他说，他需要我。

750
00:31:51.000 --> 00:31:52.200
Seat saved infinity.
座位保留到无限远。

751
00:31:52.860 --> 00:31:53.240
Aw.
噢。

752
00:31:53.860 --> 00:31:55.420
Our kids save seats.
我们的孩子会占座。

753
00:31:55.620 --> 00:31:57.140
They're still in that phase of their life.
他们还处于人生的那个阶段。

754
00:31:57.140 --> 00:31:58.740
We're like, I want that seat.
我们当时想，我想要那个座位。

755
00:31:58.940 --> 00:31:59.860
That's my seat.
那是我的座位。

756
00:32:00.300 --> 00:32:01.560
Seat saved infinity.
座位占到天荒地老。

757
00:32:02.260 --> 00:32:03.440
Dwight came to play.
德怀特是来真的。

758
00:32:03.720 --> 00:32:05.380
Well, Michael's going to come back.
嗯，迈克尔要回来了。

759
00:32:06.260 --> 00:32:08.420
His phone call was bad news, Angela.
他的电话内容很糟糕，安吉拉。

760
00:32:08.680 --> 00:32:08.880
Yeah.
是啊。

761
00:32:09.400 --> 00:32:10.300
Very bad news.
非常糟糕的消息。

762
00:32:10.880 --> 00:32:13.460
There's been a murder in Savannah.
萨凡纳发生了一起谋杀案。

763
00:32:14.080 --> 00:32:16.300
And that was the end of the act break.
那本来是幕间休息的结尾。

764
00:32:16.700 --> 00:32:18.060
It was supposed to be.
本该是那样的。

765
00:32:18.360 --> 00:32:20.160
They were supposed to go to commercial.
他们本该进广告的。

766
00:32:20.600 --> 00:32:20.820
Yeah.
是啊。

767
00:32:21.060 --> 00:32:24.240
And then when they were editing, they thought that would be stressful.
后来在剪辑时，他们觉得那样会让人压力很大。

768
00:32:24.240 --> 00:32:26.820
They thought it would be mean also to the audience.
他们还觉得那样对观众来说太刻薄了。

769
00:32:27.460 --> 00:32:34.640
But instead, we have this Michael talking head where we also see him going through his closet.
但取而代之的是，我们看到了迈克尔的访谈片段，同时看到他在翻找衣柜。

770
00:32:34.640 --> 00:32:36.080
He's looking for something.
他在找什么东西。

771
00:32:36.360 --> 00:32:37.260
His office armoire.
他的办公室衣橱。

772
00:32:37.460 --> 00:32:37.940
Yes.
没错。

773
00:32:38.220 --> 00:32:43.060
There are many games inside and we realize there has not been a real murder.
里面有很多游戏，我们意识到并没有发生真正的谋杀案。

774
00:32:43.860 --> 00:32:46.560
But we're going to play a murder mystery game.
但我们要玩一个谋杀之谜游戏。

775
00:32:46.760 --> 00:32:51.020
Yes, because Michael thinks games help distract you in stressful situations.
是的，因为迈克尔认为游戏有助于在压力大的情况下分散注意力。

776
00:32:51.440 --> 00:32:51.760
Yes.
没错。

777
00:32:52.080 --> 00:32:53.740
Did you see the games in his armoire?
你看到他衣橱里的游戏了吗？

778
00:32:53.740 --> 00:32:54.400
I did.
看到了。

779
00:32:54.600 --> 00:32:55.540
Let's read them off.
我们来读一下吧。

780
00:32:56.020 --> 00:32:56.460
All right.
好啊。

781
00:32:56.540 --> 00:32:58.040
I don't know if we wrote them in the same order.
我不知道我们列出的顺序是否一样。

782
00:32:58.740 --> 00:32:59.820
Well, you do one.
这样吧，你读一个。

783
00:32:59.880 --> 00:33:00.420
I'll do one.
我读一个。

784
00:33:00.580 --> 00:33:00.920
All right.
好的。

785
00:33:01.040 --> 00:33:01.700
Connect four.
四子棋。

786
00:33:02.200 --> 00:33:02.640
Stratego.
陆战棋。

787
00:33:03.140 --> 00:33:03.580
Operation.
手术医生。

788
00:33:04.160 --> 00:33:04.540
Trouble.
麻烦游戏。

789
00:33:05.000 --> 00:33:05.340
Sorry.
对不起。

790
00:33:05.800 --> 00:33:06.160
Risk.
风险游戏。

791
00:33:06.540 --> 00:33:06.980
Battleship.
战舰游戏。

792
00:33:07.740 --> 00:33:08.340
That's it.
就这些了。

793
00:33:08.440 --> 00:33:09.140
That's what I had.
我记得的也是这些。

794
00:33:09.360 --> 00:33:09.820
Me too.
我也是。

795
00:33:10.220 --> 00:33:15.740
Well, the game he brings in to the conference room is called Bells, Bourbon, and Bullets,
嗯，他带进会议室的游戏叫《铃铛、波本威士忌和子弹》，

796
00:33:15.780 --> 00:33:17.900
a Murder Mystery Dinner Party Game.
是一款谋杀之谜晚餐派对游戏。

797
00:33:18.180 --> 00:33:19.540
Yes, we got a lot of mail.
是的，我们收到了很多邮件。

798
00:33:19.740 --> 00:33:21.560
People wanted to know, is this a real game?
人们想知道，这是真实存在的游戏吗？

799
00:33:21.680 --> 00:33:22.420
Can I buy it?
我能买到吗？

800
00:33:22.500 --> 00:33:23.220
Can I play it?
我能玩吗？

801
00:33:23.740 --> 00:33:25.360
Well, it was a made-up game.
嗯，那是个虚构的游戏。

802
00:33:25.980 --> 00:33:31.340
The box and all the cards and the props inside were created just for our episode.
盒子、所有的卡片和里面的道具都是专门为我们这一集制作的。

803
00:33:31.780 --> 00:33:36.900
The box and the logos were designed by our new graphic designer, Henry Sane.
盒子和标志是由我们的新平面设计师亨利·塞恩设计的。

804
00:33:36.900 --> 00:33:42.920
And Phil Shea worked with Danny Chun to come up with all of the props and paraphernalia
菲尔·谢伊和丹尼·春一起构思了所有的道具和周边物品，

805
00:33:42.920 --> 00:33:44.380
that each character would have.
每个角色都会用到的那些东西。

806
00:33:44.760 --> 00:33:50.960
And Randy even shared with us that the box and cards were printed by Phil's go-to prop
