960
00:40:50.180 --> 00:40:53.840
And we didn't get to hear all the names, but he told me what they were.
我们没能听到所有的名字，但他告诉了我。

961
00:40:53.940 --> 00:40:54.580
Do you want to hear?
你想听吗？

962
00:40:54.680 --> 00:40:56.100
I absolutely do.
我当然想。

963
00:40:56.400 --> 00:40:56.960
All right.
好吧。

964
00:40:57.180 --> 00:41:00.020
Kevin is Dick Sealand.
凯文是迪克·西兰。

965
00:41:00.800 --> 00:41:01.360
Okay.
好的。

966
00:41:01.360 --> 00:41:04.160
Oscar is Chad Anuga.
奥斯卡是查德·阿努加。

967
00:41:05.500 --> 00:41:09.460
Dwight is the butler Jeeves Julep.
德怀特是管家吉夫斯·朱利普。

968
00:41:10.100 --> 00:41:12.980
Jim is George Apeach.
吉姆是乔治·阿皮奇。

969
00:41:13.600 --> 00:41:16.220
Ryan is Paul Metto.
瑞安是保罗·梅托。

970
00:41:16.940 --> 00:41:19.580
Meredith is Connie Federit.
梅雷迪斯是康妮·费德里特。

971
00:41:20.400 --> 00:41:26.260
And then, he can't remember who got assigned these characters, but he did have to write two more prop cards,
然后，他不记得这些角色分别分配给了谁，但他确实还得再写两张道具卡，

972
00:41:26.300 --> 00:41:32.180
and they were Barbie Q and Carl Earned Greens.
分别是芭比·Q和卡尔·厄恩德·格林斯。

973
00:41:32.660 --> 00:41:33.580
Earned Greens.
厄恩德·格林斯。

974
00:41:33.700 --> 00:41:37.540
Like, it's a play on collared greens, but it's like Carl Earned Greens.
就像是羽衣甘蓝（collared greens）的双关语，但写成了卡尔·厄恩德·格林斯。

975
00:41:38.900 --> 00:41:40.780
So, those are all the names you didn't hear.
所以，这些就是你们没听到的所有名字。

976
00:41:41.300 --> 00:41:45.640
Well, I did make note of all the props that went with each character.
我确实记录了每个角色对应的所有道具。

977
00:41:46.320 --> 00:41:46.540
Mm.
嗯。

978
00:41:47.260 --> 00:41:48.540
Voodoo mama Juju.
巫毒妈妈朱朱。

979
00:41:49.120 --> 00:41:53.480
Angela had a voodoo head and a hat she had to wear.
安吉拉有一个巫毒人偶头和一顶她必须戴的帽子。

980
00:41:53.720 --> 00:41:54.140
Yes.
是的。

981
00:41:54.560 --> 00:41:56.980
I did have a wardrobe fitting for that hat.
我确实为那顶帽子试过装。

982
00:41:56.980 --> 00:42:02.280
But, somewhere, there were photos of me and multiple versions of that hat, and that's the one the writers picked.
但是，在某个地方有我和那顶帽子的多个版本的照片，那是编剧们选中的那一个。

983
00:42:03.300 --> 00:42:04.860
Pam had lace gloves.
帕姆戴着蕾丝手套。

984
00:42:05.200 --> 00:42:05.600
Yes.
是的。

985
00:42:06.140 --> 00:42:08.300
Meredith had a long cigarette.
梅雷迪斯拿着一根长香烟。

986
00:42:08.540 --> 00:42:09.560
Like a cigarette holder.
就像烟嘴一样。

987
00:42:09.560 --> 00:42:10.260
Holder, yes.
烟嘴，没错。

988
00:42:10.840 --> 00:42:12.140
Kevin had a cigar.
凯文拿着雪茄。

989
00:42:12.580 --> 00:42:14.140
Phyllis had a feathery fan.
菲利斯拿着一把羽毛扇。

990
00:42:14.700 --> 00:42:18.280
Dwight had white butler gloves, and it looked like a napkin over his arm.
德怀特戴着白色管家手套，手臂上还搭着一块餐巾。

991
00:42:18.840 --> 00:42:24.300
Erin had a lace garter, and there was a deleted scene of her putting it on that didn't make it,
艾琳戴着蕾丝吊袜带，有一个她戴上它的删减片段没能放进去，

992
00:42:24.380 --> 00:42:28.100
but you see it ever so slightly at the end when she runs in the conference room.
但在最后她跑进会议室时，你可以隐约看到一点。

993
00:42:28.180 --> 00:42:28.460
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

994
00:42:28.900 --> 00:42:31.800
Andy had on men's sleeve garters.
安迪戴着男士袖箍。

995
00:42:32.120 --> 00:42:32.620
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

996
00:42:32.780 --> 00:42:36.980
And I couldn't see what everyone else had, but those were the main ones that were visible.
我没能看清其他人戴了什么，但这些是主要能看到的道具。

997
00:42:37.440 --> 00:42:41.660
So, Andy is going to try to teach Pam how to do a better accent,
所以，安迪打算教帕姆如何说出更好的口音，

998
00:42:41.800 --> 00:42:44.200
because everyone's saying she just sounds like Forrest Gump.
因为大家都说她听起来就像阿甘。

999
00:42:44.200 --> 00:42:50.320
And he is able to do, like, a Florida panhandle accent,
他能够模仿佛罗里达狭长地带的口音，

1000
00:42:50.320 --> 00:42:54.760
and then he gets into his description of a Savannah accent,
然后他开始描述萨凡纳口音，

1001
00:42:54.760 --> 00:42:57.880
where he says it's like molasses coming out of your mouth.
他说那感觉就像糖浆从你嘴里流出来一样。

1002
00:42:58.240 --> 00:42:59.400
It's so good.
太棒了。

1003
00:42:59.940 --> 00:43:03.940
Danny said they were originally planning for Andy to have a horrible accent,
丹尼说他们原本打算让安迪操着一口糟糕的口音，

1004
00:43:04.520 --> 00:43:11.440
but on the day, they realized that Ed was very good at these different accents,
但在拍摄当天，他们意识到艾德非常擅长模仿各种口音，

1005
00:43:11.600 --> 00:43:13.280
and so they rewrote it.
于是他们重写了剧本。

1006
00:43:13.280 --> 00:43:18.780
Well, he is from Georgia, and he probably has a good ear for all the accents there.
嗯，他来自佐治亚州，可能对那里的各种口音都很敏锐。

1007
00:43:19.320 --> 00:43:24.900
Interestingly enough, there was an Andy talking head in the shooting draft that did not make it.
有趣的是，拍摄剧本里原本有一段安迪的访谈片段，但最终没用上。

1008
00:43:25.160 --> 00:43:26.580
This is what it said.
内容是这样的。

1009
00:43:26.860 --> 00:43:31.280
I went to dialect camp every summer from the age 7 to 18.
我从7岁到18岁，每年夏天都去参加方言夏令营。

1010
00:43:31.660 --> 00:43:34.300
Then I was a counselor for 10 years.
后来我还当了10年的辅导员。

1011
00:43:34.820 --> 00:43:35.240
Hmm.
嗯。

1012
00:43:35.740 --> 00:43:36.260
What?
什么？

1013
00:43:36.400 --> 00:43:37.640
It was Andy's childhood.
那是安迪的童年经历。

1014
00:43:37.640 --> 00:43:43.620
So we learned in the meeting that he spent a summer in Toulouse apprenticing for a Fomagier.
我们在会议上得知他曾在图卢兹花了一个夏天当奶酪师学徒。

1015
00:43:44.000 --> 00:43:44.360
Yes.
没错。

1016
00:43:44.380 --> 00:43:48.460
Now we find out that he went to a dialect camp for years.
现在我们又发现他多年来一直参加方言夏令营。

1017
00:43:48.980 --> 00:43:54.200
Well, it's interesting, Angela, because we have wondered if deleted scenes count.
安吉拉，这很有趣，因为我们一直在想删减片段算不算数。

1018
00:43:54.460 --> 00:43:57.020
If something doesn't make it into an episode,
如果某段内容没能进入正片，

1019
00:43:57.020 --> 00:44:01.220
does it still count in that character's lore in the story?
它在角色的背景故事里还算数吗？

1020
00:44:01.440 --> 00:44:01.900
Right.
对。

1021
00:44:02.160 --> 00:44:02.280
What not?
为什么不算？

1022
00:44:02.540 --> 00:44:06.640
And sort of in the canon of the show, is it part of that?
在剧集的正史设定中，它属于其中一部分吗？

1023
00:44:06.940 --> 00:44:09.520
And we sort of said, no.
我们当时大概是说，不算。

1024
00:44:09.720 --> 00:44:09.900
No.
不算。

1025
00:44:10.420 --> 00:44:11.460
It's what aired.
播出的内容才算。

1026
00:44:11.780 --> 00:44:12.260
Yes.
是的。

1027
00:44:12.420 --> 00:44:14.680
That is what would be the show Bible.
那才是剧集的官方设定。

1028
00:44:14.680 --> 00:44:22.260
Well, I found an old article on officetally.com from 2007.
我找到了officetally.com上2007年的一篇旧文章。

1029
00:44:22.700 --> 00:44:24.260
Right when Google started.
就在谷歌刚起步的时候。

1030
00:44:24.740 --> 00:44:25.340
Right.
没错。

1031
00:44:27.900 --> 00:44:30.380
There was an interview with Greg Daniels.
里面有一篇格雷格·丹尼尔斯的采访。

1032
00:44:30.660 --> 00:44:32.020
And he talked about this?
他谈到这个了吗？

1033
00:44:32.140 --> 00:44:32.440
Yes.
谈到了。

1034
00:44:32.640 --> 00:44:33.220
What did he say?
他说了什么？

1035
00:44:33.560 --> 00:44:34.920
He said, quote,
他说，引用原话：

1036
00:44:35.180 --> 00:44:39.440
For the writers, in our minds, those scenes have happened.
对于编剧来说，在我们心中，那些场景确实发生过。

1037
00:44:39.440 --> 00:44:40.540
We wrote them.
我们写了它们。

1038
00:44:40.680 --> 00:44:41.520
We shot them.
我们拍了它们。

1039
00:44:41.520 --> 00:44:45.040
And at the last minute, I cut them in the editing room.
只是在最后一刻，我在剪辑室里把它们剪掉了。

1040
00:44:45.240 --> 00:44:49.600
But we're relying on them anyway for the mythology of the show.
但我们依然把它们作为剧集背景设定的一部分。

1041
00:44:50.540 --> 00:44:51.120
Wow.
哇。

1042
00:44:51.120 --> 00:44:51.660
Okay.
好吧。

1043
00:44:51.900 --> 00:44:56.620
So, per Greg, if it made it in the shooting draft.
所以，按照格雷格的说法，如果它出现在拍摄剧本里。

1044
00:44:56.820 --> 00:44:58.140
If we shot it.
如果我们拍了它。

1045
00:44:58.240 --> 00:44:58.800
Right.
对。

1046
00:44:59.100 --> 00:45:01.260
Then it's part of the mythology of the show.
那它就是剧集背景设定的一部分。

1047
00:45:01.440 --> 00:45:05.320
So, that would mean that, yes, Andy did spend a summer as a fromagier.
所以，这意味着安迪确实当过一个夏天的奶酪师学徒。

1048
00:45:05.760 --> 00:45:09.040
He did do this weird accent camp.
他也确实参加过那个奇怪的方言夏令营。

1049
00:45:10.140 --> 00:45:11.840
But here is the problem.
但问题来了。

1050
00:45:12.120 --> 00:45:12.380
What?
什么？

1051
00:45:13.120 --> 00:45:16.820
The exception that proves the rule would be Pam's painting.
帕姆的那幅画算是一个例外，证明了规则的存在。

1052
00:45:17.500 --> 00:45:21.480
Because Pam's painting, they shot it being destroyed.
因为帕姆的那幅画，他们拍了它被毁掉的镜头。

1053
00:45:21.760 --> 00:45:24.640
It stayed off the wall for several episodes.
它在好几集里都没挂在墙上。

1054
00:45:24.660 --> 00:45:26.560
It's still off the wall in this episode.
在这一集里，它依然没挂在墙上。

1055
00:45:26.740 --> 00:45:29.700
In this episode, there's still just golfing inspiration.
在这一集里，墙上还只是高尔夫球的装饰画。

1056
00:45:30.700 --> 00:45:32.000
But it came back.
但它后来又回来了。

1057
00:45:32.120 --> 00:45:32.520
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1058
00:45:33.640 --> 00:45:35.100
So, I don't know.
所以，我也不确定。

1059
00:45:35.580 --> 00:45:37.520
I think it's still up for debate, Greg.
我觉得这还有待商榷，格雷格。

1060
00:45:38.140 --> 00:45:38.960
Sorry, Greg.
抱歉，格雷格。

1061
00:45:39.520 --> 00:45:40.360
We don't know.
我们不知道。

1062
00:45:40.580 --> 00:45:41.020
We don't know.
我们不知道。

1063
00:45:41.020 --> 00:45:44.280
This interview does predate the destruction of the painting.
这次采访确实是在那幅画被毁之前进行的。

1064
00:45:44.660 --> 00:45:44.780
So.
所以。

1065
00:45:44.940 --> 00:45:45.260
Okay.
好吧。

1066
00:45:45.840 --> 00:45:47.840
He's allowed to change his mind on that one.
关于这一点，他有权改变主意。

1067
00:45:48.400 --> 00:45:50.600
People are pretty impressed by Andy's accents.
大家对安迪的口音印象相当深刻。

1068
00:45:50.840 --> 00:45:51.960
Kevin has a requeSt.
凯文有个请求。

1069
00:45:52.180 --> 00:45:53.240
The Swedish chef.
瑞典厨师。

1070
00:45:53.380 --> 00:45:53.660
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1071
00:45:54.160 --> 00:45:56.020
Andy's like, what province is he from?
安迪问，他是哪个省的人？

1072
00:45:56.400 --> 00:45:59.400
And Kevin says, he lives on Sesame Street, dumbass.
凯文说，他住在芝麻街，笨蛋。

1073
00:45:59.680 --> 00:46:00.060
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1074
00:46:00.060 --> 00:46:02.880
This got such a huge laugh at the table read.
这句台词在剧本围读会上引起了哄堂大笑。

1075
00:46:03.220 --> 00:46:04.980
Like, people lost their minds.
大家简直笑疯了。

1076
00:46:05.540 --> 00:46:10.820
And when the final edit of the episode came and Greg saw it, it wasn't in.
但当这一集的最终剪辑出来，格雷格看到时，这句台词被删了。

1077
00:46:11.000 --> 00:46:12.080
It got cut.
它被剪掉了。

1078
00:46:12.380 --> 00:46:12.600
Really?
真的吗？

1079
00:46:12.900 --> 00:46:15.940
And Greg was like, where's Kevin's line about Sesame Street?
格雷格当时就问，凯文关于芝麻街的那句台词去哪了？

1080
00:46:15.940 --> 00:46:18.360
He absolutely loved this line.
他非常喜欢这句台词。

1081
00:46:18.360 --> 00:46:22.540
And Greg fought really hard to have it put back in.
格雷格还极力争取把它加了回去。

1082
00:46:23.040 --> 00:46:25.440
Well, I'll have you know, Stephanie M.
好吧，我得告诉你，斯蒂芬妮·M。

1083
00:46:25.600 --> 00:46:28.720
from Salt Lake City, Utah, would like to point out
来自犹他州盐湖城的她想指出

1084
00:46:28.720 --> 00:46:31.180
that the Swedish chef does not live on Sesame Street.
瑞典厨师并不住在芝麻街。

1085
00:46:31.180 --> 00:46:32.480
He's from The Muppet Show.
他是《布偶秀》里的角色。

1086
00:46:32.800 --> 00:46:33.280
Yes.
没错。

1087
00:46:33.460 --> 00:46:35.000
Which makes the line even funnier.
这反而让那句台词更好笑了。

1088
00:46:35.160 --> 00:46:35.600
Yes.
没错。

1089
00:46:35.920 --> 00:46:37.320
Well, why don't we take a break?
好了，我们休息一下吧？

1090
00:46:37.320 --> 00:46:42.400
Because when we come back, I need to point out a line that Phyllis could not say.
因为回来之后，我得提一句菲利斯怎么也说不出来的台词。

1091
00:46:42.860 --> 00:46:43.160
Ooh.
噢。

1092
00:46:43.380 --> 00:46:45.620
And I have some things to say about Creed.
而且我还有些关于克里德的话要说。

1093
00:46:47.020 --> 00:46:47.860
We'll be back.
我们马上回来。

1094
00:46:47.860 --> 00:46:59.020
We are back.
我们回来了。

1095
00:46:59.180 --> 00:47:04.820
And as you guys re-watch this episode with us, please go to the conference room scene
当你们和我们一起重温这一集时，请留意会议室的那场戏

1096
00:47:04.820 --> 00:47:10.140
where Phyllis has to say, I overheard you asking the butler where the pistol was kept.
菲利斯必须说：我无意中听到你问管家手枪放在哪儿了。

1097
00:47:10.560 --> 00:47:11.200
Okay.
好的。

1098
00:47:12.240 --> 00:47:17.720
Jenna, do you remember every time Phyllis got to the word pistol, she started to snicker
珍娜，你还记得吗？每次菲利斯说到“手枪”这个词时，她就开始偷笑

1099
00:47:17.720 --> 00:47:20.020
and we all started to break?
然后我们所有人都忍不住笑场了？

1100
00:47:20.280 --> 00:47:20.680
No.
不记得了。

1101
00:47:21.360 --> 00:47:27.980
If you listen to it, she says, pistol, because she can barely get through that word.
如果你仔细听，她说的是“手枪”，因为她几乎没法完整说出这个词。

1102
00:47:28.240 --> 00:47:30.480
We got tickled every single time.
我们每次都被逗得不行。

1103
00:47:31.020 --> 00:47:32.100
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1104
00:47:32.260 --> 00:47:35.020
Now that you say it, I remember that.
你这么一说，我倒想起来了。

1105
00:47:35.140 --> 00:47:35.440
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1106
00:47:35.620 --> 00:47:37.840
That would happen with Phyllis in general, too.
菲利斯平时也经常这样。

1107
00:47:38.200 --> 00:47:38.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1108
00:47:38.680 --> 00:47:39.580
It was everything.
那简直绝了。

1109
00:47:39.740 --> 00:47:40.700
It was the Southern accent.
主要是那个南方口音。

1110
00:47:40.700 --> 00:47:42.160
She had to be doing the fan.
她当时肯定在扇扇子。

1111
00:47:42.260 --> 00:47:42.680
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1112
00:47:42.860 --> 00:47:47.100
And then when she said, pistol, it made me laugh.
然后当她说出“手枪”时，我忍不住笑了。

1113
00:47:47.100 --> 00:47:49.980
I remembered instantly how tickled we got.
我立刻想起我们当时笑得有多开心。

1114
00:47:50.680 --> 00:47:53.320
Well, guys, Creed is going to arrive to work.
好了，伙计们，克里德要来上班了。

1115
00:47:53.440 --> 00:47:53.940
He's late.
他迟到了。

1116
00:47:54.040 --> 00:47:54.700
He's sorry.
他很抱歉。

1117
00:47:55.080 --> 00:47:55.260
Yeah.
是啊。

1118
00:47:55.460 --> 00:47:57.340
He asks Michael, what's going on?
他问迈克尔，出什么事了？

1119
00:47:57.440 --> 00:48:03.440
And Michael says, as Caleb Crawdad, there's been a murder and you're a suspect.
迈克尔以凯莱布·克劳达德的身份说，发生了一起谋杀案，你是嫌疑人。

1120
00:48:03.960 --> 00:48:04.360
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1121
00:48:04.580 --> 00:48:06.560
And Creed is like, oh, okay, great.
克里德就说，哦，好的，太棒了。

1122
00:48:06.700 --> 00:48:07.580
Can I just have a...
我能先……

1123
00:48:07.580 --> 00:48:08.280
Let me get settled.
让我先安顿一下。

1124
00:48:08.520 --> 00:48:09.040
I'll be right back.
我马上回来。

1125
00:48:09.140 --> 00:48:09.600
I'll be right back.
我马上回来。

1126
00:48:09.860 --> 00:48:11.940
And he just hightails it right out of there.
然后他直接溜之大吉了。

1127
00:48:11.940 --> 00:48:20.040
Now, some people on some message boards think that this is an indication that Creed is the
现在，一些留言板上的网友认为这表明克里德就是

1128
00:48:20.040 --> 00:48:21.060
Scranton Strangler.
斯克兰顿勒杀手。

1129
00:48:21.700 --> 00:48:22.460
Oh.
哦。

1130
00:48:23.300 --> 00:48:23.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1131
00:48:24.000 --> 00:48:24.340
Sorry.
抱歉。

1132
00:48:24.420 --> 00:48:26.100
That reaction was like a cartoon.
那反应简直像动画片一样。

1133
00:48:26.980 --> 00:48:27.360
Oh.
哦。

1134
00:48:27.360 --> 00:48:29.460
Oh, I do declare.
哦，我敢说。

1135
00:48:30.440 --> 00:48:30.940
Yes.
是的。

1136
00:48:30.940 --> 00:48:31.860
My goodness.
天哪。

1137
00:48:33.400 --> 00:48:35.180
However, I will say this.
不过，我想说的是。

1138
00:48:35.480 --> 00:48:36.860
We see Creed leave.
我们看到克里德离开了。

1139
00:48:37.080 --> 00:48:38.660
We see him jump into a car.
我们看到他跳进了一辆车。

1140
00:48:38.860 --> 00:48:39.120
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1141
00:48:39.560 --> 00:48:43.160
I was like, oh, I think this is our first time seeing Creed's car.
我当时心想，哦，这好像是我们第一次看到克里德的车。

1142
00:48:43.160 --> 00:48:44.840
I even asked Randy about it.
我甚至还问了兰迪这件事。

1143
00:48:45.100 --> 00:48:51.400
He said that our transportation coordinator, Jesse Dutchover, rented that car from Cinema
他说我们的交通协调员杰西·达奇奥弗是从电影车辆服务公司租的那辆车。

1144
00:48:51.400 --> 00:48:52.660
Vehicle Services.
那是一辆道具车。

1145
00:48:53.320 --> 00:48:55.020
It is a picture car.
意思是专门租给剧组用于电影和电视拍摄的车辆。

1146
00:48:55.280 --> 00:48:58.780
That means cars that are rented out to productions to be in movies and TV.
而且租车点离那儿只有几个街区远。

1147
00:48:59.100 --> 00:49:01.800
And that the rental facility was just a few blocks away.
于是我们就把这辆车定为克里德的车。

1148
00:49:02.200 --> 00:49:04.540
And we established this as Creed's car.
每当我们需要拍摄克里德和他的车时，用的都是他们从那家公司租来的这辆车。

1149
00:49:04.720 --> 00:49:09.600
And whenever we needed to see Creed and his car, this was the car they rented from this facility.
直到多年后他开上了一辆保时捷。

1150
00:49:09.980 --> 00:49:12.340
Until he drove a Porsche years later.
直到多年后他开上了一辆保时捷。

1151
00:49:12.680 --> 00:49:13.040
Correct.
没错。

1152
00:49:13.160 --> 00:49:20.000
But in the future, when we see news footage of the police chasing who they think might
但在未来，当我们看到新闻片段里警察在追捕他们认为可能是

1153
00:49:20.000 --> 00:49:21.740
be the Scranton Strangler, look at the car.
“斯克兰顿勒杀手”的人时，看看那辆车。

1154
00:49:22.500 --> 00:49:23.060
Oh.
噢。

1155
00:49:23.060 --> 00:49:26.240
It is not the car that Creed jumps into right here.
那并不是克里德在这里跳进去的那辆车。

1156
00:49:26.700 --> 00:49:33.540
Now, does Creed have many cars at his disposal after his work as the Scranton Strangler?
那么，克里德在当过“斯克兰顿勒杀手”之后，手头还有很多车吗？

1157
00:49:33.660 --> 00:49:34.580
Possibly, yes.
有可能，是的。

1158
00:49:34.800 --> 00:49:40.000
But I did just want to point out that there's a little bit of a car thing going on.
但我只是想指出，这里确实有点关于车的小细节。

1159
00:49:40.000 --> 00:49:45.300
I mean, Creed also, we have found out, lives under his desk and has a home in Canada.
我是说，我们还发现克里德住在办公桌底下，在加拿大还有一个家。

1160
00:49:45.560 --> 00:49:48.140
So, anything can happen with Creed.
所以，克里德身上什么事都可能发生。

1161
00:49:48.180 --> 00:49:50.240
I have some things to share as well.
我也有一些事情要分享。

1162
00:49:50.840 --> 00:49:56.900
Greg said that Creed running to his car was actually a lot harder to shoot than it looks.
格雷格说，克里德跑向他那辆车的镜头其实比看起来难拍得多。

1163
00:49:57.080 --> 00:49:57.480
Really?
真的吗？

1164
00:49:57.480 --> 00:49:59.040
First of all, the timing of it.
首先是时机的问题。

1165
00:49:59.160 --> 00:50:00.700
I mean, Creed had to really book it.
我是说，克里德必须真的全速冲刺。

1166
00:50:01.040 --> 00:50:02.560
He had to run to the car.
他得跑向车子。

1167
00:50:02.680 --> 00:50:03.500
He had to jump in.
他得跳进去。

1168
00:50:03.620 --> 00:50:09.040
And then doing this back out and pull out move with a car as big as a Lincoln Town Car,
然后还要驾驶像林肯城市轿车这么大的车，做出倒车再开走的动作，

1169
00:50:09.160 --> 00:50:11.260
which is what it is, was not easy.
也就是他开的那辆，这并不容易。

1170
00:50:11.260 --> 00:50:15.120
So, this quick little moment actually took a little bit of planning.
所以，这个短暂的小瞬间其实花了不少心思去策划。

1171
00:50:15.600 --> 00:50:22.620
And, lady, it's at this moment I realized that Creed, the character, and me in real life have a little something in common.
而且，女士，就在那一刻我意识到，克里德这个角色和我本人有一个共同点。

1172
00:50:22.940 --> 00:50:23.720
What's that?
是什么？

1173
00:50:23.960 --> 00:50:26.560
We have both driven Lincoln Town Cars.
我们都开过林肯城市轿车。

1174
00:50:27.180 --> 00:50:29.360
Oh, you had a Lincoln Town Car once?
噢，你曾经有一辆林肯城市轿车？

1175
00:50:29.360 --> 00:50:34.600
My grandmother's car was a green Lincoln Town Car with a white top.
我祖母的车是一辆绿色的林肯城市轿车，配着白色的车顶。

1176
00:50:35.000 --> 00:50:40.920
And my grandmother is who taught me how to drive because in the summers I would go stay with my grandparents for a visit.
是我祖母教我开车的，因为夏天的时候我会去祖父母家住上一段时间。

1177
00:50:41.240 --> 00:50:46.440
And when I was turning 16, she took me out in her enormous Lincoln Town Car.
在我快满16岁时，她开着她那辆巨大的林肯城市轿车带我出去。

1178
00:50:46.700 --> 00:50:48.520
And that's what I learned to drive a car in.
我就是在那辆车上学会开车的。

1179
00:50:49.140 --> 00:50:49.620
Wow.
哇。

1180
00:50:50.280 --> 00:50:53.160
You know, I learned how to drive in an enormous car as well.
你知道吗，我也是在一辆巨大的车上学会开车的。

1181
00:50:53.280 --> 00:50:54.520
What was the enormous car?
是什么巨大的车？

1182
00:50:54.660 --> 00:50:57.160
It was a 1978 Pontiac Catalina.
是一辆1978年的庞蒂亚克卡特琳娜。

1183
00:50:57.560 --> 00:50:58.020
Hey!
嘿！

1184
00:50:58.020 --> 00:50:59.520
That was a big, long car.
那可是一辆又大又长的车。

1185
00:50:59.600 --> 00:51:00.280
That was a big, long car.
那可是一辆又大又长的车。

1186
00:51:00.380 --> 00:51:02.100
My grandmother had pedal extenders.
我祖母有踏板延长器。

1187
00:51:02.580 --> 00:51:03.460
So, that was good.
所以，那挺好的。

1188
00:51:03.680 --> 00:51:05.420
So, I wasn't right up on the steering wheel.
这样我就不用整个人贴在方向盘上了。

1189
00:51:05.500 --> 00:51:07.740
You sort of had to learn in your grandmother's car.
你算是得在祖母的车上学开车。

1190
00:51:08.260 --> 00:51:08.620
Why?
为什么？

1191
00:51:08.820 --> 00:51:09.440
Because I'm short?
因为我个子矮吗？

1192
00:51:10.000 --> 00:51:10.480
Well, yeah.
嗯，是的。

1193
00:51:10.720 --> 00:51:12.500
Those pedal extenders really helped you out.
那些踏板延长器真的帮了你大忙。

1194
00:51:12.640 --> 00:51:13.280
They were very helpful.
它们非常有帮助。

1195
00:51:13.460 --> 00:51:17.320
Apparently, I made my mom stressed out when she rode with me to teach me how to drive.
显然，我妈教我开车时，我让她感到压力很大。

1196
00:51:17.840 --> 00:51:19.180
So, she gave it to your grandma?
所以她就把这事交给你祖母了？

1197
00:51:19.300 --> 00:51:21.360
Yeah, my dad was like, I'm not getting in the car with her.
对，我爸当时说，我可不跟她一起坐车。

1198
00:51:21.560 --> 00:51:23.920
So, my grandmother said, I'll teach her to drive.
于是我祖母说，我来教她开车。

1199
00:51:24.060 --> 00:51:24.800
And she did.
然后她就教了。

1200
00:51:24.980 --> 00:51:27.920
Well, as your BFF, who's ridden in many cars with you,
好吧，作为你的好闺蜜，我坐过你开的很多次车，

1201
00:51:28.020 --> 00:51:28.900
you're a great driver.
你开车技术真棒。

1202
00:51:29.140 --> 00:51:29.780
Thank you.
谢谢。

1203
00:51:30.020 --> 00:51:30.220
Yeah.
是啊。

1204
00:51:30.460 --> 00:51:32.080
No pedal extenders anymore either.
也不再需要踏板延长器了。

1205
00:51:32.380 --> 00:51:33.820
The seat goes all the way up.
座椅可以调到最前面。

1206
00:51:34.180 --> 00:51:35.440
Although, I wouldn't mind.
不过，我倒是不介意。

1207
00:51:36.000 --> 00:51:36.460
Really?
真的吗？

1208
00:51:36.740 --> 00:51:37.020
Yeah.
真的。

1209
00:51:37.200 --> 00:51:39.120
Because then you're not so close to the steering wheel.
因为那样你就不会离方向盘那么近了。

1210
00:51:39.240 --> 00:51:39.440
Yeah.
是啊。

1211
00:51:40.060 --> 00:51:42.340
So, now we have a little romance in the kitchen.
所以，现在厨房里上演了一段小浪漫。

1212
00:51:42.720 --> 00:51:45.080
Andy and Erin, they're chatting.
安迪和艾琳，他们正在聊天。

1213
00:51:45.200 --> 00:51:46.500
They're still doing their accents.
他们还在用那种口音说话。

1214
00:51:46.960 --> 00:51:49.460
But he asks her out on a date, and she says yes.
但他约她出去约会，她答应了。

1215
00:51:50.140 --> 00:51:55.300
But then later in the conference room, other people start asking her out on a date, and
但后来在会议室里，其他人也开始约她出去，然后

1216
00:51:55.300 --> 00:51:56.220
she's saying yes.
她都答应了。

1217
00:51:56.420 --> 00:51:58.480
And then Andy is like, oh, wait.
于是安迪心想，哦，等等。

1218
00:51:58.480 --> 00:52:00.560
Was she just in character in the kitchen?
她在厨房里只是在演戏吗？

1219
00:52:00.860 --> 00:52:00.910
Yeah.
是啊。

1220
00:52:00.940 --> 00:52:02.380
Or are we really going on a date?
还是说我们真的要约会了？

1221
00:52:02.580 --> 00:52:04.320
Did I ask out Naughty Nellie?
我约的是那个淘气内莉吗？

1222
00:52:04.420 --> 00:52:05.620
Or did I ask out Erin?
还是我约的是艾琳？

1223
00:52:06.660 --> 00:52:12.880
Well, in the conference room at 12 minutes, 36 seconds, there is a really good shot of
嗯，在会议室场景12分36秒的时候，有一个非常清晰的镜头

1224
00:52:13.680 --> 00:52:18.800
Kevin's character card, where you can very plainly see that his name is Dixieland.
拍到了凯文的角色卡，你可以很清楚地看到他的名字叫迪克西兰。

1225
00:52:19.400 --> 00:52:23.360
And he also has an extra prop in this scene.
而且他在这个场景里还有一个额外的道具。

1226
00:52:23.360 --> 00:52:24.680
He's got a wad of money.
他手里拿着一叠钱。

1227
00:52:24.920 --> 00:52:25.900
Oh, yes.
哦，没错。

1228
00:52:26.060 --> 00:52:29.900
It's said in the script that he was one of the richest men in all of Savannah.
剧本里说他是萨凡纳最富有的人之一。

1229
00:52:30.160 --> 00:52:30.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1230
00:52:30.760 --> 00:52:34.120
Well, so much so that he walks around carrying a wad of money.
富有到他走来走去都随身带着一叠钱。

1231
00:52:35.260 --> 00:52:36.800
Oscar interrupts the game.
奥斯卡打断了游戏。

1232
00:52:37.000 --> 00:52:42.140
He shares that he received an email from corporate instructing the accounting department
他说他收到了一封来自总部的邮件，指示会计部门

1233
00:52:42.140 --> 00:52:44.620
to stop all payments to vendors.
停止向所有供应商付款。

1234
00:52:44.960 --> 00:52:45.320
Wow.
哇。

1235
00:52:45.520 --> 00:52:46.180
That's serious.
那可是大事。

1236
00:52:46.400 --> 00:52:46.800
Yeah.
是啊。

1237
00:52:46.800 --> 00:52:53.300
Well, Michael insists that Oscar give no more details unless he is speaking in character.
迈克尔坚持要求奥斯卡除非用角色口吻，否则不许透露更多细节。

1238
00:52:53.740 --> 00:52:54.140
Yeah.
是啊。

1239
00:52:54.160 --> 00:52:56.420
He cannot use his Yankee accent, Michael says.
迈克尔说，他不能用他的北方口音。

1240
00:52:57.460 --> 00:52:59.040
So Oscar tries.
于是奥斯卡尝试了。

1241
00:52:59.300 --> 00:53:04.000
To give important news about the company as a Southern character.
用南方角色的口吻来传达关于公司的重要消息。

1242
00:53:04.540 --> 00:53:05.400
We got mail.
我们有邮件了。

1243
00:53:05.800 --> 00:53:06.120
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1244
00:53:06.800 --> 00:53:08.100
Van Melflury on this one.
这封邮件来自范·梅尔弗里。

1245
00:53:08.400 --> 00:53:12.120
Starting with Zach M from Venice Center, New York.
首先是来自纽约威尼斯中心的扎克·M的提问。

1246
00:53:12.120 --> 00:53:18.440
Does Oscar struggle with a Southern accent in real life, or was this just more of his brilliant acting?
奥斯卡在现实生活中真的很难模仿南方口音吗，还是这只是他精湛演技的体现？

1247
00:53:19.140 --> 00:53:20.940
Zach, it was just brilliant acting.
扎克，那纯粹是精湛的演技。

1248
00:53:21.060 --> 00:53:24.480
A hundred percent amazing acting job by Oscar.
奥斯卡百分之百精彩的表演。

1249
00:53:24.480 --> 00:53:32.220
We did about six takes of this, and Danny Chun spoke about this in an interview with officetelly.com.
我们拍了大约六次，丹尼·春在接受officetelly.com采访时提到了这一点。

1250
00:53:32.660 --> 00:53:38.180
He reminded me that at first, Oscar was doing a really deep voice.
他提醒我，起初奥斯卡用的是一种非常低沉的声音。

1251
00:53:38.240 --> 00:53:38.580
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1252
00:53:38.580 --> 00:53:43.260
And it was the last take where he did the super high voice.
那是最后一次拍摄，他用了那种超高的嗓音。

1253
00:53:43.460 --> 00:53:43.680
Yeah.
没错。

1254
00:53:43.860 --> 00:53:45.000
That we used in the show.
我们把它用在了剧里。

1255
00:53:45.520 --> 00:53:47.220
None of us were expecting it.
我们谁也没想到会这样。

1256
00:53:47.520 --> 00:53:50.400
We had gotten used to his low voice Southern accent.
我们都已经习惯他那种低沉的南方口音了。

1257
00:53:50.760 --> 00:53:51.400
That's right.
确实。

1258
00:53:51.840 --> 00:53:59.720
We had a fan question from Jenny F in Amarillo, Texas, and many others who wanted to know how did we keep a straight face during this scene.
有位来自德克萨斯州阿马里洛的珍妮·F，还有许多观众问我们，拍这场戏时是怎么忍住不笑场的。

1259
00:54:00.280 --> 00:54:01.280
Oh, we did not.
哦，我们根本没忍住。

1260
00:54:01.520 --> 00:54:01.800
No.
没忍住。

1261
00:54:02.040 --> 00:54:03.540
Especially not on that last take.
尤其是最后那次拍摄。

1262
00:54:03.700 --> 00:54:04.520
Not the one you see.
不是你们在正片里看到的那次。

1263
00:54:04.740 --> 00:54:05.240
No.
没有。

1264
00:54:05.480 --> 00:54:11.820
When he came in in that higher falsetto, and he's talking about the greenback, we were on the floor.
当他用那种高亢的假声走进来，说着关于美钞的事时，我们都笑趴在地上了。

1265
00:54:12.560 --> 00:54:15.720
Even Steve broke, and Steve never breaks.
连史蒂夫都笑场了，他可是从不笑场的。

1266
00:54:16.020 --> 00:54:18.520
It made it onto the season six bloopers.
那段被收录进了第六季的NG花絮里。

1267
00:54:18.860 --> 00:54:21.440
I asked Cassie to pull it so we could hear it.
我让卡西把它找出来，这样我们就能听听了。

1268
00:54:22.260 --> 00:54:27.020
This here plantation is running low on greenbacks.
这个种植园的美钞快用完了。

1269
00:54:27.020 --> 00:54:34.660
Um, we ain't got no money to pay the people who sell us the seeds and dirt, manure.
嗯，我们没钱付给那些卖种子、泥土和肥料的人了。

1270
00:54:35.080 --> 00:54:36.580
I can't do this, Michael.
我演不下去了，迈克尔。

1271
00:54:37.680 --> 00:54:38.260
Basically.
基本上就是这样。

1272
00:54:45.180 --> 00:54:46.940
You can sort of hear Steve.
你多少能听到史蒂夫的声音。

1273
00:54:47.140 --> 00:54:48.980
I can recognize everybody's different laughs.
我能认出每个人的笑声。

1274
00:54:49.040 --> 00:54:49.560
I do, too.
我也能。

1275
00:54:49.800 --> 00:54:50.840
I hear John.
我听到了约翰的笑声。

1276
00:54:51.200 --> 00:54:53.800
I hear definitely Brian and Steve.
我肯定听到了布莱恩和史蒂夫的。

1277
00:54:54.220 --> 00:54:54.860
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1278
00:54:54.860 --> 00:54:58.520
Oh, man, I re-watched the bloopers for that as well.
天哪，我也重温了那段NG花絮。

1279
00:54:58.980 --> 00:55:03.700
And from the camera angle from our backs, my head is just bent over.
从我们背后的摄像机角度看，我的头都低垂下去了。

1280
00:55:03.860 --> 00:55:05.280
Like, I'm bent over.
就像这样，我整个人都弯下去了。

1281
00:55:05.900 --> 00:55:17.120
I have to say, whenever Oscar and Steve were paired together in a scene, just, I don't know what it was.
我得说，每当奥斯卡和史蒂夫在戏里搭档时，我也不知道为什么。

1282
00:55:17.260 --> 00:55:21.900
Those two, I think because they were the two that never broke, they got each other.
他们俩，我想是因为他们是那两个从不笑场的人，所以他们很懂对方。

1283
00:55:22.040 --> 00:55:22.700
They really did.
确实如此。

1284
00:55:22.700 --> 00:55:27.500
Yeah, I wish, you know, there were more Oscar-Michael moments.
是啊，我真希望当时能有更多奥斯卡和迈克尔的对手戏。

1285
00:55:27.740 --> 00:55:35.160
Like, in re-watching, I'm like, gosh, man, I really wish that Oscar had to, like, do a sales call with Michael or something.
重温的时候，我心想，天哪，我真希望奥斯卡能和迈克尔一起去跑个销售什么的。

1286
00:55:35.400 --> 00:55:37.260
Well, I know there's some good ones coming up.
嗯，我知道后面还有些精彩的戏份。

1287
00:55:37.360 --> 00:55:37.720
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1288
00:55:38.320 --> 00:55:42.600
This news from Oscar really bumps people out, and they go back to work.
奥斯卡带来的这个消息让大家很沮丧，于是他们回去工作了。

1289
00:55:42.760 --> 00:55:43.060
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1290
00:55:43.340 --> 00:55:45.920
Also, the murderer is revealed on the tape.
此外，凶手在录像带里被揭露了。

1291
00:55:46.120 --> 00:55:47.120
It was Phyllis.
是菲利斯。

1292
00:55:47.120 --> 00:55:51.080
And she was really bummed because she felt like she was doing a good job.
她当时很沮丧，因为她觉得自己演得很好。

1293
00:55:52.300 --> 00:55:57.880
Andy wants to figure out if he asked Aaron out or if he asked out Naughty Nelly.
安迪想弄清楚他约的是亚伦，还是那个“淘气内莉”。

1294
00:55:58.180 --> 00:55:58.460
Right.
对。

1295
00:55:58.640 --> 00:56:00.760
So they have this great scene at front reception.
所以他们在前台有一场很棒的戏。

1296
00:56:01.020 --> 00:56:08.860
I thought Ed and Ellie did such a great job just playing two people who like each other but are afraid to admit it.
我觉得艾德和艾莉演得太棒了，完美诠释了两个互相喜欢却不敢承认的人。

1297
00:56:08.980 --> 00:56:09.380
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1298
00:56:09.860 --> 00:56:10.580
I agree.
我同意。

1299
00:56:10.880 --> 00:56:16.320
It ultimately ends up that neither of them admit that it was real when it was real for both of them.
最终结果是，明明两人都是真心的，却谁也不肯承认那是真的。

1300
00:56:16.320 --> 00:56:16.980
Yeah.
是啊。

1301
00:56:17.600 --> 00:56:24.620
So it's not going to happen yet, but we are solidifying the information that they're into each other.
所以这事儿还没成，但我们正在确认他们确实对彼此有意思。

1302
00:56:25.180 --> 00:56:27.180
Michael insists the game isn't over.
迈克尔坚持认为游戏还没结束。

1303
00:56:27.420 --> 00:56:30.780
He is now, I think he's in a full spiral.
他现在，我觉得他整个人都陷入了混乱。

1304
00:56:31.100 --> 00:56:32.620
He will not break character.
他就是不肯出戏。

1305
00:56:33.280 --> 00:56:38.860
Danny talked about this and the challenge of writing for Michael when Michael isn't his true self.
丹尼谈到了这一点，以及当迈克尔不是真实的自我时，为他写剧本所面临的挑战。

1306
00:56:38.980 --> 00:56:39.380
Oh.
哦。

1307
00:56:39.620 --> 00:56:43.540
He said he had to write for Michael as Caleb Crawdad.
他说他必须以“凯莱布·克劳达德”的身份来为迈克尔写台词。

1308
00:56:45.060 --> 00:56:54.700
And Greg compared this episode to grief counseling when Michael was unaware of what was motivating him and the episode was playing out in his subconscious.
格雷格把这一集比作“悲伤辅导”，当时迈克尔并不知道是什么在驱动他，而这一集是在他的潜意识中展开的。

1309
00:56:54.920 --> 00:57:02.400
And he said this episode is a variation of that where Michael is not sure what's motivating him, but he's locked into this character.
他说这一集是那种情况的变体，迈克尔不确定是什么在驱动他，但他已经完全沉浸在这个角色里了。

1310
00:57:02.400 --> 00:57:03.960
That's really interesting.
那真的很有趣。

1311
00:57:04.500 --> 00:57:09.920
You know, Pam and Jim are going to have a talking head where they ask the question, has Michael snapped?
你知道，帕姆和吉姆会有一个采访镜头，他们会问：迈克尔是不是疯了？

1312
00:57:10.180 --> 00:57:11.760
Is he stuck in character?
他是被困在角色里了吗？

1313
00:57:12.280 --> 00:57:13.540
What's going on?
到底发生了什么？

1314
00:57:13.980 --> 00:57:16.260
I noticed something in this talking head.
我在这段采访里注意到了一件事。

1315
00:57:16.500 --> 00:57:16.940
What?
什么？

1316
00:57:16.940 --> 00:57:24.960
I am wearing the same outfit that I wore in Double Date, which was last week's episode.
我穿的这套衣服和我在上一集《双重约会》里穿的一模一样。

1317
00:57:25.360 --> 00:57:26.960
It's exactly the same.
完全一样。

1318
00:57:27.160 --> 00:57:33.320
I kind of noticed it earlier in the episode, but this talking head solidified it for me.
我在这一集早些时候就注意到了，但这个采访镜头让我确定了这一点。

1319
00:57:33.900 --> 00:57:34.540
Yeah.
是啊。

1320
00:57:34.700 --> 00:57:37.200
Now that you say it, it's the exact same outfit.
你这么一说，确实是同一套衣服。

1321
00:57:37.440 --> 00:57:38.560
Exactly the same.
完全一样。

1322
00:57:38.560 --> 00:57:45.560
It's that very kind of dark gray shirt with that lighter gray blazer.
就是那件深灰色的衬衫配浅灰色的西装外套。

1323
00:57:46.400 --> 00:57:46.620
Yes.
没错。

1324
00:57:46.860 --> 00:57:47.280
Thank you.
谢谢。

1325
00:57:47.420 --> 00:57:48.520
I was trying to get the words.
我刚才还在想怎么形容呢。

1326
00:57:48.660 --> 00:57:55.680
The only thing that's different is that in Double Date, I'm wearing some little hoop earrings that I'm not wearing in this episode.
唯一不同的是，在《双重约会》里我戴了一副小圆耳环，而这一集没戴。

1327
00:57:56.240 --> 00:57:58.800
I tried to figure out how did this happen?
我试着弄清楚这是怎么回事？

1328
00:57:59.260 --> 00:58:05.480
Why would Alicia put the same outfit in my trailer on back-to-back weeks?
为什么艾丽西亚会连续两周在我的拖车里放同一套衣服？

1329
00:58:06.220 --> 00:58:07.420
Well, she didn't.
嗯，她没这么做。

1330
00:58:07.420 --> 00:58:10.180
I have a Mom Detectives moment.
我有个“妈妈侦探”时刻。

1331
00:58:10.340 --> 00:58:10.640
What?
什么？

1332
00:58:10.800 --> 00:58:11.620
What'd you find out?
你发现了什么？

1333
00:58:11.780 --> 00:58:17.660
I found out that we filmed these episodes in a different order than they aired.
我发现我们拍摄这些剧集的顺序和播出的顺序不一样。

1334
00:58:17.920 --> 00:58:23.700
We originally filmed Double Date, then Koi Pond, then Murder.
我们最初拍摄的是《双重约会》，然后是《锦鲤池》，接着是《谋杀》。

1335
00:58:24.120 --> 00:58:24.880
Oh.
哦。

1336
00:58:25.320 --> 00:58:27.500
So, there was a week in between.
所以，中间隔了一周。

1337
00:58:28.060 --> 00:58:33.260
They aired as Koi Pond first, then Double Date, then Murder.
但播出顺序是先播《锦鲤池》，然后是《双重约会》，最后是《谋杀》。

1338
00:58:34.040 --> 00:58:40.740
So, I had gone up to the bigger belly bump, the belly bee, and it was only meant for these three episodes.
当时我的孕肚已经变大了，那个假肚子只打算用在这三集里。

1339
00:58:41.560 --> 00:58:44.820
And we had to tailor the clothes to the bump.
我们必须根据孕肚来裁剪衣服。

1340
00:58:44.980 --> 00:58:51.400
So, I think Alicia was trying to get a little extra mileage out of my bee bump wardrobe.
所以我猜艾丽西亚是想让我的孕妇装多发挥点余热。

1341
00:58:51.400 --> 00:58:58.180
And she thought, well, as long as I throw an episode in between, we won't notice that Pam has recycled this outfit.
她觉得，只要中间插播一集，我们就不会注意到帕姆重复穿了这套衣服。

1342
00:58:58.420 --> 00:59:00.800
But then they ended up airing back-to-back.
但结果它们被安排连续播出了。

1343
00:59:01.040 --> 00:59:02.720
So, Pam's in the same clothes.
所以，帕姆就穿了同一套衣服。

1344
00:59:02.820 --> 00:59:04.980
Same clothes, two weeks in a row.
连续两周穿同一套衣服。

1345
00:59:05.200 --> 00:59:06.860
Good Mom Detective catch.
好一个“妈妈侦探”式的发现。

1346
00:59:06.860 --> 00:59:07.460
Thank you.
谢谢。

1347
00:59:08.100 --> 00:59:12.420
You know Dunder Mifflin closing is really going to hit Pam and Jim hard.
你知道邓德·米夫林公司的倒闭对帕姆和吉姆打击真的很大。

1348
00:59:12.420 --> 00:59:13.480
They both work there.
他们都在那儿工作。

1349
00:59:13.600 --> 00:59:16.220
They're married and both working at the same company.
他们结婚了，而且在同一家公司上班。

1350
00:59:16.220 --> 00:59:17.060
And expecting a baby.
还要迎接一个宝宝。

1351
00:59:17.060 --> 00:59:17.940
With a baby on the way.
孩子快要出生了。

1352
00:59:18.080 --> 00:59:18.380
Yes.
是的。

1353
00:59:18.380 --> 00:59:19.280
I know.
我知道。

1354
00:59:19.660 --> 00:59:25.200
And they're talking about that in Jim's office when Michael busts in and he's like, come on, Deb.
当时他们正在吉姆的办公室里谈论这件事，迈克尔突然闯了进来，他说，来吧，黛布。

1355
00:59:25.460 --> 00:59:26.280
We need you.
我们需要你。

1356
00:59:26.420 --> 00:59:27.140
We need you.
我们需要你。

1357
00:59:27.820 --> 00:59:29.100
And Pam goes.
然后帕姆去了。

1358
00:59:29.300 --> 00:59:36.260
At 17 minutes, two seconds, if you're curious what is splattered on the floor by Meredith's head, that's roast beef.
在17分02秒的时候，如果你好奇梅雷迪思头旁边地板上溅的是什么，那是烤牛肉。

1359
00:59:36.620 --> 00:59:40.780
It's from the little lunch platter that is there on the table.
来自桌上那个小午餐拼盘。

1360
00:59:40.980 --> 00:59:44.180
You can see all the roast beef has been placed on the floor.
你可以看到所有的烤牛肉都掉在地上了。

1361
00:59:45.000 --> 00:59:47.480
Jim has really lost his patience at this point.
吉姆此时已经彻底失去了耐心。

1362
00:59:47.700 --> 00:59:49.540
And he demands to speak to Michael.
他要求和迈克尔谈谈。

1363
00:59:49.740 --> 00:59:53.220
And Michael snaps back at him so hard.
而迈克尔对他进行了猛烈的回击。

1364
00:59:53.280 --> 00:59:54.600
He's like, you shut up.
他说，你闭嘴。

1365
00:59:55.220 --> 00:59:55.760
Yeah.
没错。

1366
00:59:56.020 --> 00:59:58.420
And we have one of those drama moments.
然后我们迎来了一个戏剧性的时刻。

1367
00:59:59.200 --> 01:00:00.240
Here's the thing.
事情是这样的。

1368
01:00:00.620 --> 01:00:03.820
We've been wondering, is Michael losing it?
我们一直在想，迈克尔是不是疯了？

1369
01:00:03.940 --> 01:00:04.940
Has he gone crazy?
他是不是精神失常了？

1370
01:00:05.220 --> 01:00:09.400
And here's where you realize he's actually quite lucid.
但就在这里你意识到他其实非常清醒。

1371
01:00:09.520 --> 01:00:10.920
And this is a choice.
这是一种选择。

1372
01:00:10.920 --> 01:00:17.020
He is choosing to lose himself and help the office lose themselves in this game.
他选择让自己沉浸其中，并帮助办公室里的其他人也沉浸在这个游戏中。

1373
01:00:17.420 --> 01:00:19.080
It is a strategy.
这是一种策略。

1374
01:00:19.620 --> 01:00:23.040
During all of this, David Wallace finally calls back.
就在这一切发生时，大卫·华莱士终于回电了。

1375
01:00:23.760 --> 01:00:24.980
Jim takes the call.
吉姆接了电话。

1376
01:00:25.220 --> 01:00:27.880
I thought Andy Buckley did such a great job.
我觉得安迪·巴克利演得太棒了。

1377
01:00:27.920 --> 01:00:38.120
Because you can just hear how distracted slash worried slash trying to, like, put out a bunch of fires, like his day, you know?
因为你能听出他那种心烦意乱、忧心忡忡，又试图四处救火的状态，就像他的一天那样，你懂吗？

1378
01:00:38.120 --> 01:00:38.500
Yeah.
是的。

1379
01:00:39.020 --> 01:00:39.540
Yeah.
没错。

1380
01:00:39.640 --> 01:00:43.420
He was just sitting back in the annex at Kelly's desk making this phone call.
他当时就坐在附楼凯利的办公桌后面打这个电话。

1381
01:00:43.560 --> 01:00:45.000
In real life, that's where he was.
在现实生活中，他当时就在那里。

1382
01:00:45.260 --> 01:00:47.860
Well, everyone knows that Jim has just taken this call.
好吧，大家都知道吉姆刚接了那个电话。

1383
01:00:48.120 --> 01:00:50.620
And they're so anxious about what he's going to say.
他们非常担心他会说什么。

1384
01:00:50.980 --> 01:00:54.040
And there's no really anything good to say.
其实也没什么好消息可说。

1385
01:00:54.220 --> 01:00:57.220
And so Jim decides to join Michael.
所以吉姆决定加入迈克尔。

1386
01:00:57.540 --> 01:01:01.420
And he's like, turns out there's been another murder.
他说，结果又发生了一起谋杀案。

1387
01:01:02.020 --> 01:01:05.540
And the look on Michael's face of, like, oh, thank God.
迈克尔脸上的表情仿佛在说，哦，谢天谢地。

1388
01:01:05.840 --> 01:01:06.800
He's with me.
他站在我这边。

1389
01:01:07.540 --> 01:01:09.180
Well, I love their talking head.
我喜欢他们的采访片段。

1390
01:01:09.740 --> 01:01:12.240
Michael has this line that rang so true to me.
迈克尔有句台词让我深有感触。

1391
01:01:12.380 --> 01:01:15.940
He says, today is the hardest I've worked in a long, long time.
他说，今天是我很久很久以来工作最努力的一天。

1392
01:01:16.280 --> 01:01:17.980
That was a pitch from Steve.
那是史蒂夫提议的。

1393
01:01:18.720 --> 01:01:19.880
Yeah, it's good.
是啊，这很棒。

1394
01:01:20.080 --> 01:01:20.980
It's so good.
太棒了。

1395
01:01:21.160 --> 01:01:23.120
I didn't know that he pitched that.
我不知道那是他提议的。

1396
01:01:23.320 --> 01:01:23.640
Yeah.
是的。

1397
01:01:24.080 --> 01:01:27.760
I mean, I also just thought of how hard Steve worked this week.
我是说，我也想到了史蒂夫这周工作有多辛苦。

1398
01:01:28.080 --> 01:01:28.360
Yeah.
没错。

1399
01:01:29.480 --> 01:01:31.300
Like, that was a hard week.
那真是艰难的一周。

1400
01:01:31.460 --> 01:01:31.780
Yeah.
是啊。

1401
01:01:32.460 --> 01:01:36.880
Well, now Andy, Michael, and Dwight are in a three-way standoff with, like, finger guns.
好了，现在安迪、迈克尔和德怀特正陷入一场三方对峙，他们用手指比作枪指着对方。

1402
01:01:37.140 --> 01:01:37.480
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1403
01:01:37.700 --> 01:01:39.460
They're, like, pointed at each other.
他们就像是互相指着对方。

1404
01:01:39.720 --> 01:01:40.180
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1405
01:01:40.440 --> 01:01:44.020
I guess Jim shares that Andy revealed himself to be a double agent.
我想吉姆应该分享了安迪暴露自己是双重间谍的事。

1406
01:01:44.040 --> 01:01:45.680
And then so was Dwight.
然后德怀特也是。

1407
01:01:45.780 --> 01:01:47.380
And as it turns out, so was Michael.
结果发现，迈克尔也是。

1408
01:01:48.120 --> 01:01:49.320
Also, it's 6 o'clock.
而且现在已经六点了。

1409
01:01:49.400 --> 01:01:50.800
And Jim would really like to go home.
吉姆真的很想回家了。

1410
01:01:50.800 --> 01:01:55.540
Um, yeah, but guess who he needs to get out of the conference room?
嗯，对，但你猜他需要把谁从会议室里弄出来？

1411
01:01:55.700 --> 01:01:57.480
Pam is part of this standoff.
帕姆也参与了这场对峙。

1412
01:01:57.620 --> 01:01:58.380
She is.
没错。

1413
01:01:58.580 --> 01:02:00.420
Her finger guns are drawn as well.
她的手指枪也拔出来了。

1414
01:02:00.580 --> 01:02:04.240
And she says to Jim, grab the keys, start the car.
她对吉姆说，去拿钥匙，发动车子。

1415
01:02:04.460 --> 01:02:07.580
She's going to slowly back out of the conference room.
她打算慢慢地从会议室退出去。

1416
01:02:08.040 --> 01:02:13.120
And then the three-way standoff turns into a dramatic shootout.
然后那场三方对峙就变成了一场戏剧性的枪战。

1417
01:02:13.400 --> 01:02:15.160
Everyone's writhing on the floor.
每个人都在地板上痛苦地扭动。

1418
01:02:15.500 --> 01:02:18.020
We had a fan question from Caroline P.
我们收到了一个来自夏威夷火奴鲁鲁的卡罗琳·P的粉丝提问。

1419
01:02:18.200 --> 01:02:19.260
in Honolulu, Hawaii.
在夏威夷火奴鲁鲁。

1420
01:02:19.260 --> 01:02:23.440
For the tag at the end, how much of that scene was scripted?
关于结尾的彩蛋，那一幕有多少是写在剧本里的？

1421
01:02:23.520 --> 01:02:28.100
And how much of it was just Steve, Ed, and Rain improvising and having fun with it?
又有多少是史蒂夫、艾德和雷恩即兴发挥、自娱自乐的？

1422
01:02:28.700 --> 01:02:29.920
Well, I'll tell you what.
嗯，我来告诉你吧。

1423
01:02:30.680 --> 01:02:35.520
In the script, it ends with Pam backing out of the conference room.
剧本里，那一幕是以帕姆从会议室退出去结束的。

1424
01:02:35.680 --> 01:02:39.160
It was supposed to just end on a standoff.
本来应该就在对峙中结束的。

1425
01:02:39.360 --> 01:02:39.620
Yeah.
是啊。

1426
01:02:39.620 --> 01:02:47.280
And then on the day, they started doing the shootout, all shooting each other, and this
结果拍摄当天，他们开始演起枪战，互相射击，然后就

1427
01:02:47.280 --> 01:02:48.500
is how it ended up being.
变成了现在这个样子。

1428
01:02:48.840 --> 01:02:53.980
Greg shared that when the guys fell on the ground and were, like, convulsing and everything,
格雷格分享说，当他们倒在地上，在那儿抽搐什么的的时候，

1429
01:02:54.320 --> 01:02:55.300
that was just them.
那完全是他们自己的发挥。

1430
01:02:55.380 --> 01:02:56.260
They were just having fun.
他们只是玩得很开心。

1431
01:02:56.360 --> 01:02:58.360
He said it was like little kids getting to play.
他说那就像小孩子在玩耍一样。

1432
01:02:58.520 --> 01:02:58.820
Yeah.
没错。

1433
01:02:59.080 --> 01:03:00.240
It looked like it.
看起来确实像。

1434
01:03:00.280 --> 01:03:00.720
It did.
确实是。

1435
01:03:00.720 --> 01:03:05.400
Well, at 20 minutes, 44 seconds, I wanted to point out one thing.
嗯，在20分44秒的时候，我想指出一件事。

1436
01:03:05.780 --> 01:03:08.960
The reveal of Pam is so great.
帕姆出场的那一刻太棒了。

1437
01:03:09.220 --> 01:03:12.880
And Greg shared what really made that happen was our camera operator, Matt Sohn.
格雷格分享说，真正促成那一幕的是我们的摄像师马特·索恩。

1438
01:03:13.060 --> 01:03:19.580
His ability to whip around in a circle like that is what really captured the moment.
他那种能迅速转圈的能力，才真正捕捉到了那一刻。

1439
01:03:20.000 --> 01:03:21.860
Matt and Randall were so amazing.
马特和兰德尔真是太厉害了。

1440
01:03:22.120 --> 01:03:25.500
So whenever we can give a shout out to them, way to go, Matt Sohn.
所以每当我们有机会提到他们时，干得好，马特·索恩。

1441
01:03:25.500 --> 01:03:28.660
We got another fan question from Patricia B.
我们收到了另一个来自俄克拉荷马州帕特里夏·B的粉丝提问，她说，珍娜，你有多

1442
01:03:28.860 --> 01:03:31.020
in Oklahoma who said, Jenna, how much did
享受最后那一幕，就是你在会议室里用手指枪

1443
01:03:31.020 --> 01:03:35.240
you enjoy that final scene when you were in the conference room doing your finger gun
对峙的时候？

1444
01:03:35.240 --> 01:03:35.940
standoff?
那太有趣了。

1445
01:03:36.440 --> 01:03:37.600
It was so fun.
而且那成了我一个非常流行的表情包。

1446
01:03:37.760 --> 01:03:40.500
And it's like a very popular meme of me.
是啊。

1447
01:03:40.740 --> 01:03:40.980
Yeah.
你知道，上面写着，我可不会为此背锅。

1448
01:03:41.260 --> 01:03:43.900
You know, that says, I'm not going down for this.
是啊。

1449
01:03:44.020 --> 01:03:44.180
Yeah.
那句台词。

1450
01:03:44.340 --> 01:03:44.960
That line.
那句台词。

1451
01:03:45.760 --> 01:03:47.300
It was so funny.
那太搞笑了。

1452
01:03:47.300 --> 01:03:55.580
I remember the direction from Greg was like, you need to act like you are 100% invested
我记得格雷格给的指导是，你需要表现得百分之百投入

1453
01:03:55.580 --> 01:03:56.020
in this.
到这件事里。

1454
01:03:56.140 --> 01:03:57.560
Like, this is real in your mind.
就好像，在你心里这一切都是真的。

1455
01:03:57.560 --> 01:03:58.520
You have to get out.
你必须逃出去。

1456
01:03:58.760 --> 01:04:01.240
You have to get out and you're going to get out safe.
你必须逃出去，而且你要安全地逃出去。

1457
01:04:01.680 --> 01:04:04.040
I was like, all right, let's do it.
我就想，好吧，那就来吧。

1458
01:04:04.220 --> 01:04:06.260
And you got to be in a mini action movie.
然后你就拍了一部迷你动作片。

1459
01:04:06.360 --> 01:04:06.960
I did.
没错。

1460
01:04:07.240 --> 01:04:07.400
On The Office.
在《办公室》里。

1461
01:04:07.840 --> 01:04:08.600
I did.
没错。

1462
01:04:09.640 --> 01:04:11.140
Well, there you have it.
好吧，就是这样。

1463
01:04:11.240 --> 01:04:12.620
That is murder.
那是谋杀。

1464
01:04:12.980 --> 01:04:16.120
I want to give a big thank you to Danny Chun for all of his details.
我要非常感谢丹尼·春提供的所有细节。

1465
01:04:16.120 --> 01:04:19.840
He said you can find him at Danny Chun on Twitter.
他说你可以在推特上通过 Danny Chun 找到他。

1466
01:04:20.220 --> 01:04:24.920
He's got a bunch of fun stuff coming up, but he said it's going to be a while, not till
他有很多有趣的作品即将推出，但他说是还要等上一阵子，要到

1467
01:04:24.920 --> 01:04:28.000
the summer, but we'll post all about it when it's there.
夏天，但等到了时候我们会发布相关消息的。

1468
01:04:28.180 --> 01:04:33.360
Well, of course, we always want to give a big shout out and lots of love to Randy Cordray
当然，我们每周都要向兰迪·科德雷表示感谢并送上我们的爱，

1469
01:04:33.940 --> 01:04:35.820
every week answering our questions.
感谢他回答我们的问题。

1470
01:04:35.960 --> 01:04:36.760
We love you, Randy.
我们爱你，兰迪。

1471
01:04:37.500 --> 01:04:38.320
All right, you guys.
好了，各位。

1472
01:04:38.440 --> 01:04:42.060
Well, we're taking next week off for spring break, but we'll be back the week after with
我们要休息一周过春假，但我们会在两周后回来，

1473
